gn, exponent forms, Infinity, NaN, empty,\n     very long digit strings, subnormals, overflow to inf\n   - js_grisu2 / js_fmtexp / js_itoa / jsV_numbertostring: 0, -0, integers, fractions,\n     powers of ten, huge/tiny exponents, NaN, +/-Inf, values needing 17 sig digits\n   - jsV_numbertoint32/uint32/int16/uint16/integer: 0, -0, NaN, +/-Inf, exact ints,\n     fractions truncating toward zero, values wrapping modulo 2^32 / 2^16, huge magnitudes\n   - regexp: literal, ., char classes, negated classes, ranges, anchors ^ $, \\b \\B,\n     escapes \\d \\D \\w \\W \\s \\S, backrefs, alternation, groups, non-capturing (?:),\n     lookahead (?= (?!, quantifiers * + ? {n} {n,} {n,m}, greedy vs non-greedy,\n     nested groups, counted subgroups, empty matches, REG_MAXSUB boundary\n   - JS value/stack shapes: undefined/null/bool/number/string/object/array/function,\n     empty vs 1 vs many elements, sparse arrays, large array lengths\n3. The FULL set of public entry points INCLUDING the lowest-level exported ones,\n   not only convenience wrappers. Run this to see the exported list:\n     nm -D --defined-only /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno/c_src/build/libmujs.so | awk '{print $3}' | sort -u\n   Cover the jsU_*, jsV_*, jsY_*, js_reg*, js_strtod/js_strtol/js_grisu2/js_itoa/\n   js_fmtexp/js_isarrayindex/js_utflen/js_utfptrtoidx/js_runeat families plus the\n   mujs.h stack API and the jsB_init*/jsC_*/jsP_* builtins-and-compiler entry points.\n\nWrite ONE ROW per meaningful COMBINATION that the C treats differently (the cross-product\nof the axes, PRUNED to combinations the code actually distinguishes), in this exact format:\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n\nRules:\n- Every row must be concretely testable: the \"configuration\" cell must say exactly what\n  to set and what input shape to feed, precisely enough that someone can write the 