\tint\t\tislowerrune(Rune c);\n46\tint\t\tisupperrune(Rune c);\n47\tRune\t\ttolowerrune(Rune c);\n48\tRune\t\ttoupperrune(Rune c);\n49\tconst Rune*\ttolowerrune_full(Rune c);\n50\tconst Rune*\ttoupperrune_full(Rune c);\n51\t\n52\t#endif\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017qJdwcipwmF5VcSEZrRNRR","session_id":"365846c7-7961-47ff-8218-f2422469d650","uuid":"8c3f38eb-76d7-49b2-93c6-5c73220f6087","timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:43:56.806Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"CONFIGS part 1: numeric/utf/lexer"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6lcywfdyekj5rbdaacqnhx64iyz4e65oathvtox6kjmb3hqvpumq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Uk1rKJqkmq4n94NL8zq5zM","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"CONFIGS part 2: regexp","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno\n\nRead ONLY the C source in `c_src/` (NEVER modify it). Produce exactly ONE file:\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno/translation/CONFIGS_part2.md`\n\nThis is PART 2 of a CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE for MuJS. PART 2 covers ONLY the regular\nexpression engine and its JS binding:\n  - `c_src/src/regexp.c` and `c_src/src/regexp.h`  (js_regcomp, js_regcompx, js_regexec,\n    js_regfree, js_regfreex, and every internal node type / opcode the parser emits)\n  - `c_src/src/jsregexp.c`  (js_newregexp, js_toregexp, js_RegExp_prototype_exec,\n    jsB_initregexp, and the JS_REGEXP_G/I/M -> REG_ICASE/REG_NEWLINE mapping)\n\nMethod: read `regexp.c` end to end. Enumerate:\n1. Every compile flag combination: cflags = 0, REG_ICASE(1), REG_NEWLINE(2), and 1|2.\n   Also the JS-level flags JS_REGEXP_G(1)/JS_REGEXP_I(2)/JS_REGEXP_M(4) and all 8 combos,\n   and how jsregexp.c maps them onto cflags.\n2. Every exec flag: eflags = 0 and REG_NOTBOL(4).\n3. Every distinct PATTERN SHAPE the parser/compiler branches on. Go through the parser\n   functions and the emitted opcode/node kinds and list one row per construct:\n   literal chars, `.`, char class `[...]`, negated class `[^...]`, class ranges,\n   class escapes inside a class, anchors `^` `$`, word boundaries `\\b` `\\B`,\n   escapes `\\d \\D \\w \\W \\s \\S \\n \\r \\t \\f \\v \\0 \\xHH \\uHHHH \\cX \\<octal>`,\n   backreferences `\\1`..`\\9`, alternation `|`, capturing group `(...)`,\n   non-capturing `(?:...)`, positive lookahead `(?=...)`, negative lookahead `(?!...)`,\n   quantifiers `*` `+` `?` `{n}` `{n,}` `{n,m}`, non-greedy variants `*?` `+?` `??` `{n,m}?`,\n   nested groups, nested quantifiers, empty alternatives, empty pattern.\n   For EACH construct, also give a concrete subject string that matches and one that\n   does not, so the row is directly testable via js_regexec.\n4. Every SUBJECT shape: empty string, match at offset 0, match in the middle,\n   no match, multiple possible matches (leftmost-longest vs leftmost-first semantics\n   -- check which the C implements), subject with embedded newlines (interacts with\n   REG_NEWLINE), non-ASCII / multi-byte UTF-8 subject, subject with >REG_MAXSUB(16)\n   groups in the pattern, exactly 16 groups, 15 groups.\n5. The `js_regcompx`/`js_regfreex` custom-allocator entry points vs the plain\n   `js_regcomp`/`js_regfree` (which use the default allocator) -- one row each, and a\n   row for a custom allocator with a non-NULL ctx.\n\nExact required format (markdown table, grouped under `##` headings):\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n\nRules:\n- Number rows sequentially starting at 1.\n- The configuration cell must be concrete: give the exact pattern string, cflags value,\n  eflags value, and subject string. Cite the `regexp.c:NNN` line for the branch.\n- Derive from the source only; do not guess at features. If a construct is NOT supported\n  by this engine, do not create a valid-path row for it (that belongs in ERRORS.md).\n- Aim for 70-130 rows.\n- Start the file with `# CONFIGS — Part 2: regexp engine`.\n\nIf too large for one write, Write the file then append with more writes.\nFinish by running `wc -l` and `grep -c '^|'` on the file and report both numbers."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2719,"cache_read_input_tokens":82524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2719,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_to