{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hyyzqkotrxqypfmtlhvojzxsjftvckfupkbgaqwh2ryhsbavd64q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01ErDNkvW8dV5oTFHWLsJRiL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno/translation/ERRORS.md","content":"# MuJS Error-Surface Table\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/src/*.c`, `c_src/src/*.h`, `c_src/include/mujs.h`.\nEvery row is one distinct rejection/error branch that the C source actually checks.\n\n## Legend\n\n**Error/sentinel conventions verified in the source:**\n\n* **regexp compile** — `js_regcompx()` / `js_regcomp()` install a `setjmp` landing pad\n  (`regexp.c:903`). All compile-time rejections go through\n  `static void die(struct cstate *g, const char *message)` which stores the static message\n  string in `g->error` and `longjmp(g->kaboom, 1)` (`regexp.c:67-71`). The landing pad then\n  does `if (errorp) *errorp = g.error;`, frees partial allocations, and **returns `NULL`**\n  (`regexp.c:903-912`). On success `*errorp = NULL` and the `Reprog*` is returned\n  (`regexp.c:984-985`). If `errorp == NULL` the message is discarded but `NULL` is still\n  returned. `js_regcomp()` is just `regcompx(default_alloc, NULL, ...)` (`regexp.c:1007-1010`).\n* **regexp match** — `js_regexec()` returns **`0` = match**, **`1` = no match**,\n  **`-1` = recursion limit exceeded** (`regexp.c:1075-1076`, `regexp.c:1239`; the `-1` is\n  produced by `match()` when `depth > REG_MAXREC`). There is no `errorp`.\n* **regexp free** — `js_regfree(NULL)` / `js_regfreex(alloc, ctx, NULL)` are silent no-ops\n  (`regexp.c:990`).\n* **JS-level throws** — the `js_error` family is generated by the `DERROR` macro\n  (`jserror.c:84-99`): `vsnprintf` into a **256-byte** `buf`, build an Error object of the\n  matching prototype, then `js_throw(J)`. `js_throw()` unwinds to the innermost\n  `js_try`/`js_savetry` frame via `longjmp` (`jsrun.c:146