her than a stack error.\n* **UTF-8 decode** — `jsU_chartorune` never fails: on malformed input it sets\n  `*rune = Runeerror (0xFFFD)` and **returns 1** (`utf.c:127-129`).\n* **`js_newstate`** returns **`NULL`** on allocation failure or on a throw during\n  `jsB_init` (`jsstate.c:199`, `:217`, `:226`).\n* **`assert()`** — 9 total in the library (see rows below); `NDEBUG` builds elide them.\n\n**Real limit constants (grepped, not guessed):**\n\n| constant | value | file:line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `JS_STACKSIZE` | 4096 | jsi.h:81 |\n| `JS_ENVLIMIT` | 1024 | jsi.h:84 |\n| `JS_TRYLIMIT` | 64 | jsi.h:87 |\n| `JS_ARRAYLIMIT` | `1<<26` (67108864) | jsi.h:91 |\n| `JS_GCFACTOR` | 5.0 | jsi.h:103 |\n| `JS_ASTLIMIT` | 400 | jsi.h:107 |\n| `JS_STRLIMIT` | `1<<28` (268435456) | jsi.h:111 |\n| `js_Instruction` | `unsigned short` | jsi.h:119 |\n| `REG_MAXSUB` | 16 | regexp.h:35 |\n| `REPINF` | 255 | regexp.c:16 |\n| `REG_MAXPROG` | `32<<10` (32768) | regexp.c:18 |\n| `REG_MAXREC` | 4096 | regexp.c:21 |\n| `REG_MAXSPAN` | 64 (→ 32 ranges/class) | regexp.c:24 |\n| `REG_MAXCLASS` | 128 | regexp.c:27 |\n| `UTFmax` / `Runeerror` / `Runemax` | 4 / 0xFFFD / 0x10FFFF | utf.h:79-83 |\n| `maxExponent` (js_strtod) | 511 | jsdtoa.c:558 |\n| `JS_REGEXP_G/I/M` | 1/2/4 | mujs.h:82-84 |\n| `REG_ICASE/REG_NEWLINE/REG_NOTBOL` | 1/2/4 | regexp.h:23-28 |\n| `JS_READONLY/DONTENUM/DONTCONF` | 1/2/4 | mujs.h:89-91 |\n| `JS_STRICT` | 1 | mujs.h:77 |\n\n---\n\n## 1. `js_regcomp` / `js_regcompx` — compile rejections (all return `NULL`, set `*errorp`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1 | `js_regcomp` / `hex()` | `\\xZZ` or `\\uZZZZ` — escape digit not in `[0-9a-fA-F]` (regexp.c:101) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid escape sequence\"` |\n| 2 | `js_regcomp` / `dec()` | `a{x}` — non-digit inside `{...}` quantifier (regexp.c:108) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid quantifier\"` |\n| 3 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | pattern ends with a bare `\\` (regexp.c:127-128) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n| 4 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | pattern ends with `\\c` (no control letter) (regexp.c:137-138) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n| 5 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | `\\x` with fewer than 2 bytes remaining (regexp.c:142-143) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n| 6 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | `\\u` with fewer than 4 bytes remaining (regexp.c:152-153) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n| 7 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | identity escape of a unicode letter or `_`, e.g. `\\q`, `\\_`, `\\é` — not in `ESCAPES \"BbDdSsWw^$\\\\.*+?()[]{}|-0123456789\"` (regexp.c:167-170) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid escape character\"` |\n| 8 | `js_regcomp` / `lexcount()` | `{`-quantifier min reaches `REPINF` (255), e.g. `a{255}` (regexp.c:185-186) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"numeric overflow\"` |\n| 9 | `js_regcomp` / `lexcount()` | `{`-quantifier max reaches `REPINF` (255), e.g. `a{1,255}` (regexp.c:199-200) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"numeric overflow\"` |\n| 10 | `js_regcomp` / `newcclass()` | more than `REG_MAXCLASS` (128) character classes in one pattern (regexp.c:212-213) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"too many character classes\"` |\n| 11 | `js_regcomp` / `addrange()` | range with `a > b`, e.g. `[z-a]` (regexp.c:223-224) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid character class range\"` |\n| 12 | `js_regcomp` / `addrange()` | more than `REG_MAXSPAN/2` = 32 disjoint spans in one class (`cc->end + 2 >= cc->spans + 64`) (regexp.c:252-253) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"too many character class ranges\"` |\n| 13 | `js_regcomp` / `lexclass()` | EOF before closing `]`, e.g. `[abc` (regexp.c:321-322) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated character class\"` |\n| 14 | `js_regcomp` / `newrep()` | `max == REPINF` over an atom that can match empty, e.g. `(?:)*`, `(a*)*` (regexp.c:492-493) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"in