return `-1` |\n| 117 | `jsY_tokenstring` | `token < 0` or `token >= nelem(tokenstring)` (jslex.c:68) | returns `\"<unknown>\"` |\n| 118 | `jsY_tokenstring` | `token` in the 0x80..0xFF hole where the table holds `0` (jslex.c:42-49, 69) | returns `\"<unknown>\"` |\n\n## 6. String index helpers (`jsstring.c`, `jsrun.c`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 119 | `js_runeat` | `i` beyond the end of `s` (hits the NUL) (jsstring.c:25-27) | returns **`EOF`** (`-1`) |\n| 120 | `js_runeat` | `i < 0` on entry — `while (i >= 0)` never runs, `rune` stays `EOF` (jsstring.c:22-23, 46) | returns **`EOF`** (`-1`) |\n| 121 | `js_runeat` | `i` lands on the *first* UTF-16 unit of an astral char (`i == -2` after the decrement) (jsstring.c:38-41) | returns the high surrogate `0xD800 + ((rune-0x10000) >> 10)` |\n| 122 | `js_runeat` | `i` lands on the *second* UTF-16 unit of an astral char (jsstring.c:43-44) | returns the low surrogate `0xDC00 + ((rune-0x10000) & 0x3FF)` |\n| 123 | `js_utflen` | astral (`>= 0x10000`) characters (jsstring.c:65-66) | counted as **2** (UTF-16 length, not code-point count) |\n| 124 | `js_utflen` | malformed UTF-8 — relies on `chartorune` returning 1 with `0xFFFD` (jsstring.c:64) | each bad byte counts as 1; never loops forever (advance is always `>= 1`) |\n| 125 | `js_utfptrtoidx` | `p < s` — the `while (s < p)` loop never runs (jsstring.c:77) | returns **`0`** |\n| 126 | `js_utfptrtoidx` | `p` not on a character boundary, or `p` past the NUL (jsstring.c:77-91) | walks past the terminator; no bounds check — caller must pass a pointer inside `s` |\n| 127 | `js_isarrayindex` | empty string `\"\"` (jsrun.c:512-513) | returns **`0`**, `*idx` untouched |\n| 128 | `js_isarrayindex` | `\"0\"` exactly (jsrun.c:516-517) | returns **`1`**, `*idx = 0` |\n| 129 | `js_isarrayindex` | leading zero with more digits, e.g. `\"00\"`, `\"01\"`