ithout a `CHECKSTACK`; can point past the stack |\n| 140 | `js_remove` | resolved `idx < BOT` or `idx >= TOP` (jsrun.c:413-416) | `Error \"stack error!\"` |\n| 141 | `js_replace` | resolved `idx < BOT` or `idx >= TOP` (jsrun.c:428-431) | `Error \"stack error!\"` |\n| 142 | `js_insert` | **any** call (jsrun.c:422-425) | unconditional `Error \"not implemented yet\"` |\n| 143 | `js_rot2` | fewer than 2 values on the stack — **no check**, reads `STACK[TOP-1]`, `STACK[TOP-2]` (jsrun.c:459-464) | out-of-bounds read/write below `BOT`; no error raised |\n| 144 | `js_rot3` | fewer than 3 values — no check (jsrun.c:466-473) | out-of-bounds access; no error |\n| 145 | `js_rot4` | fewer than 4 values — no check (jsrun.c:475-483) | out-of-bounds access; no error |\n| 146 | `js_rot2pop1` | fewer than 2 values — no check (jsrun.c:485-490) | out-of-bounds access; `TOP` may drop below `BOT` |\n| 147 | `js_rot3pop2` | fewer than 3 values — no check (jsrun.c:492-497) | out-of-bounds access |\n| 148 | `js_rot` | `n` larger than the number of values, or `n <= 0` (jsrun.c:499-506) | no bounds check; `n <= 0` writes `STACK[TOP-1] = tmp` (harmless), `n` too large under-runs the stack |\n| 149 | `js_dup` | empty frame — reads `STACK[TOP-1]` with no lower-bound check (jsrun.c:444-449) | out-of-bounds read |\n| 150 | `js_currentfunction` | called at top level (`BOT == 0`) (jsrun.c:204-207) | pushes `undefined` instead of a function |\n| 151 | `js_currentfunctiondata` | called at top level (`BOT == 0`) (jsrun.c:213-215) | returns **`NULL`** |\n| 152 | `js_currentfunctiondata` | `BOT > 0` but `STACK[BOT-1]` is not a C function object (jsrun.c:212-213) | unchecked `u.object->u.c.data` read — type confusion |\n| 153 | `js_gettop` | any state (jsrun.c:400-403) | `TOP - BOT`; never errors |\n\n## 8. Public API type coercions that throw (`jsrun.c`, `jsvalue.c`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|-------------------------------------