stack overflow\"`** (jsrun.c:14-19) — note this throw itself needs a try frame, so at top level it panics/aborts |\n| 177 | `js_savetrypc` (bytecode `OP_TRY`) | `J->trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` (64) (jsrun.c:1439-1440) | throws literal `\"exception stack overflow\"` |\n| 178 | `js_endtry` | `J->trytop == 0` (unbalanced `js_endtry`) (jsrun.c:1460-1461) | `Error \"endtry: exception stack underflow\"` |\n| 179 | `js_throw` | `J->trytop == 0` (no active try frame) (jsrun.c:1483-1486) | calls `J->panic(J)`; if panic returns, **`abort()`** |\n| 180 | `js_malloc` | `J->memlimit > 0 && size >= J->memlimit` (jsrun.c:53-56) | `js_outofmemory()` → throws literal `\"out of memory\"` |\n| 181 | `js_malloc` | allocator returns `NULL` (jsrun.c:59-61) | throws literal `\"out of memory\"` |\n| 182 | `js_realloc` | `J->memlimit > 0 && size >= J->memlimit` (jsrun.c:66-70) | throws literal `\"out of memory\"` |\n| 183 | `js_realloc` | allocator returns `NULL` (jsrun.c:72-74) | throws literal `\"out of memory\"` — the old pointer is **leaked/lost** |\n| 184 | interpreter loop | `J->runlimit == 1` after decrementing per instruction (jsrun.c:1601-1604) | `js_runlimit()` → throws literal `\"script ran too long\"` |\n| 185 | `js_setlimit` | `runlimit <= 0` / `memlimit <= 0` (jsrun.c:224-228, checks at :53 and :66 are `> 0`) | limit disabled, no error |\n| 186 | `js_pcall` | any throw inside `js_call(J, n)` (jsrun.c:1407-1417) | stack trimmed to `savetop+1` holding the error value; **returns `1`** |\n| 187 | `js_pconstruct` | any throw inside `js_construct(J, n)` (jsrun.c:1394-1404) | stack trimmed to `savetop+1`; **returns `1`** |\n| 188 | `js_pcall`/`js_pconstruct` | try stack already full — they call `js_try` directly with **no `js_ptry` pre-check** (jsrun.c:1396, 1409) | `js_savetry` throws `\"exception stack overflow\"` *out of* the p-function instead of returning 1 |\n| 189 | `js_eval` | top of stack is not a string (jsrun.c:1387-1388) | returns immediately, leaving the value in place (no er