\n| 202 | `js_ptry` (used by rows 203-210) | `J->trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` (64) (jsstate.c:6-11) | pushes literal `\"exception stack overflow\"` on the stack and returns `1` — **without** using a jmp_buf |\n| 203 | `js_ploadstring` | try stack already full (jsstate.c:38-39) | returns **`1`**, error string on the stack |\n| 204 | `js_ploadstring` | any lex/parse/compile throw for `source` (jsstate.c:40-41) | returns **`1`**, SyntaxError object on the stack |\n| 205 | `js_dostring` | try stack already full (jsstate.c:141-145) | `js_report(J, \"exception stack overflow\")`, pops, returns **`1`** |\n| 206 | `js_dostring` | any throw during load or call (jsstate.c:146-150) | `js_report(J, js_trystring(J,-1,\"Error\"))`, pops, returns **`1`** |\n| 207 | `js_trystring` | try stack full, or `js_tostring` throws (jsstate.c:50-57) | pops 1, returns the caller-supplied `error` pointer |\n| 208 | `js_trynumber` | try stack full, or `js_tonumber` throws (jsstate.c:66-73) | pops 1, returns the caller-supplied `error` double |\n| 209 | `js_tryinteger` | try stack full, or `js_tointeger` throws (jsstate.c:82-89) | pops 1, returns the caller-supplied `error` int |\n| 210 | `js_tryboolean` | try stack full, or `js_toboolean` throws (jsstate.c:98-105) | pops 1, returns the caller-supplied `error` int |\n| 211 | `js_tryrepr` | any throw in `js_torepr` (jsrepr.c:275-282) — note: **no `js_ptry` pre-check**, so a full try stack throws out | pops 1, returns the caller-supplied `error` pointer |\n| 212 | `js_report` | `J->report == NULL` (after `js_setreport(J, NULL)`) (jsstate.c:166-170) | message silently dropped, no output, no error |\n| 213 | `js_loadstringx` (`js_loadstring`, `js_loadeval`) | throw from `jsP_parse` or `jsC_compilescript` (jsstate.c:116-119) | `jsP_freeparse(J)` then rethrow (`js_throw`) — the AST arena is always released |\n| 214 | `js_atpanic` | `panic == NULL` (jsstate.c:159-164) | installs `NULL`; a later top-level `js_throw` then goes straight to `abort()` (jsrun.c:1483-1486) |\n\n## 11. Property access / array limits (`jsrun.c`, `jsproperty.c`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 215 | `jsR_setarrayindex` (`js_setindex`, `js_setproperty` on arrays) | `k + 1 > JS_ARRAYLIMIT` (1<<26 = 67108864) (jsrun.c:675-676) | `RangeError \"array too large\"` |\n| 216 | `jsR_setarrayindex` | called on a non-simple (unflattened) array (jsrun.c:673) | **`assert(obj->u.a.simple)`** |\n| 217 | `jsR_setarrayindex` | negative `k` (jsrun.c:674) | **`assert(k >= 0)`** |\n| 218 | `jsR_setarrayindex` | `newlen` more than one past the flat length (jsrun.c:678) | **`assert(newlen == obj->u.a.flat_length + 1)`** |\n| 219 | `jsR_setproperty` on array `\"length\"` | assigned value is not an exact non-negative integer (`newlen != rawlen \\|\\| newlen < 0`), e.g. `a.length = 1.5` or `-1` (jsrun.c:704-707) | `RangeError \"invalid array length\"` |\n| 220 | `jsR_setproperty` on array `\"length\"` | `newlen > JS_ARRAYLIMIT` (1<<26) (jsrun.c:708-709) | `RangeError \"array too large\"` |\n| 221 | `jsR_setproperty` | **strict** mode, target property has a getter but no setter (jsrun.c:772-773) | `TypeError \"setting property '%s' that only has a getter\"` |\n| 222 | `jsR_setproperty` | **strict** mode, `transient` target (i.e. `js_setproperty` on a primitive) and the property does not exist (jsrun.c:781-783) | `TypeError \"cannot create property '%s' on transient object\"` |\n| 223 | `jsR_setproperty` | property has `JS_READONLY`, **strict** mode (jsrun.c:798-800) | `TypeError \"'%s' is read-only\"` |\n| 224 | `jsR_setproperty` | `JS_CSTRING` object: write to `\"length\"` or to a valid index `0 <= k < u.s.length`, strict (jsrun.c:735-741 → :798) | `TypeError \"'%s' is read-only\"` |\n| 225 | `jsR_setproperty` | `JS_CREGEXP` object: write to `source`/`global`/`ignoreCase`/`multiline`, strict (jsrun.c:744-748 → :798) | `TypeError \