s `\"length\"` (jsarray.c:16-20 → jsrun.c:707) | `RangeError \"invalid array length\"` |\n\n## 12. Lexer rejections (`jslex.c`) — all become `SyntaxError \"<file>:<line>: <msg>\"`\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 251 | `jsY_unescape` (identifiers) | `\\` not followed by `u`, or `\\u` with fewer than 4 hex digits, e.g. `var \\x41;` (jslex.c:181-192) | `SyntaxError \"unexpected escape sequence\"` |\n| 252 | `lexhex` | `0x` / `0X` with no hex digit following, e.g. `0x` (jslex.c:254-255) | `SyntaxError \"malformed hexadecimal number\"` |\n| 253 | `lexnumber` | `0` immediately followed by a decimal digit (legacy octal), e.g. `010` (jslex.c:350-351) | `SyntaxError \"number with leading zero\"` |\n| 254 | `lexnumber` | `e`/`E` with no digits after (and no sign digits), e.g. `1e`, `1e+` (jslex.c:376-377) | `SyntaxError \"missing exponent\"` |\n| 255 | `lexnumber` | number immediately followed by an identifier-start char, e.g. `123abc`, `1_0` (jslex.c:380-381) | `SyntaxError \"number with letter suffix\"` |\n| 256 | `lexescape` | `\\` at EOF inside a string (jslex.c:398-399) | `SyntaxError \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n| 257 | `lexescape` → `lexstring` | `\\uXXXX` or `\\xXX` with a non-hex digit — `lexescape` returns `1` (jslex.c:402-411) and `lexstring` converts it (jslex.c:442-443) | `SyntaxError \"malformed escape sequence\"` |\n| 258 | `lexstring` | EOF or a raw newline before the closing quote, e.g. `\"abc` (jslex.c:439-440) | `SyntaxError \"string not terminated\"` |\n| 259 | `jsY_expect` macro | expected literal character absent (used by `lexstring` jslex.c:449, `lexregexp` jslex.c:510, `lexjsonstring` jslex.c:830, JSON keywords jslex.c:862-870) (jslex.c:177) | `SyntaxError \"expected '%c'\"` |\n| 260 | `lexregexp` | EOF or newline inside the regexp body, e.g. `/abc` (jslex.c:489-490) | `SyntaxError \"regular expression no