"` → the bare test fails, `\"+Infinity\"` matches, `e = s+9` (jsvalue.c:235-236) | [ ] |\n| 159 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string = `\"-Infinity\"` → `-INFINITY`, `e = s+9` (jsvalue.c:237-238) | [ ] |\n| 160 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string = `\"Infinityfoo\"` → prefix matches but `*e` is `'f'` after the trailing-space skip → NaN (jsvalue.c:233, 241-242) | [ ] |\n| 161 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string = `\"12  \\n\"` → trailing whitespace/newline skip loop, then `*e == 0` → 12 (jsvalue.c:241-243) | [ ] |\n| 162 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string = `\"\"` (empty) → `js_stringtofloat` returns 0 with `*ep == s`, `*e == 0` → result 0, NOT NaN (jsvalue.c:240-243; jsvalue.c:217-219) | [ ] |\n| 163 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string = `\"   \"` (whitespace only) → skipped to NUL → 0 (jsvalue.c:230, 242) | [ ] |\n| 164 | `jsV_stringtonumber` | string = `\"12abc\"` → `js_stringtofloat` scan ends at `'a'`, `*e != 0` → NaN (jsvalue.c:242) | [ ] |\n| 165 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\"12\"` → no `'.'`, no `'e'` → `isflt == 0` → unsigned `js_strtol(s, ..., 10)` branch (jsvalue.c:195-199, 214-215) | [ ] |\n| 166 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\"-12\"` → `isflt == 0` and `*s == '-'` → `-js_strtol(s+1, ..., 10)` (the sign is applied manually) (jsvalue.c:210-211) | [ ] |\n| 167 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\"+12\"` → `*s == '+'` → `js_strtol(s+1, ...)` (jsvalue.c:212-213) | [ ] |\n| 168 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\"-\"` alone → `isflt == 0`, `js_strtol(\"\")` returns 0, `end == e == s+1` → returns `-0.0` and `*ep` at NUL, so `jsV_stringtonumber(\"-\")` yields -0 rather than NaN (jsvalue.c:196, 210-211, 217-219) | [ ] |\n| 169 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\"1.5\"` → `'.'` sets `isflt = 1` → `js_strtod` branch (jsvalue.c:198, 206-207) | [ ] |\n| 170 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\"1.\"` → `'.'` with no following digits; `isflt = 1`, scan end and `js_strtod` end both at NUL → 1.0 (jsvalue.c:198-199, 217) | [ ] |\n| 171 | `js_stringtofloat` | string = `\".5\"` → leading `'.