tch; the flag is inert for patterns without `^` | [ ] |\n| 46 | js_regexec | eflags=REG_NOTBOL(4), pattern `a$` , cflags=0, subject `\"a\"` → match — `REG_NOTBOL` never reaches `I_EOL` (regexp.c:1186-1197) | [ ] |\n| 47 | js_regexec | eflags=REG_NOTBOL(4), pattern `\\ba`, cflags=0, subject `\"abc\"` → match — `I_WORD` uses `sp > bol` only and ignores `REG_NOTBOL` (regexp.c:1198-1204) | [ ] |\n| 48 | js_regexec | eflags=REG_ICASE(1) on a prog compiled with cflags=0: `eflags` is OR-ed into `prog->flags` (regexp.c:1239). Pattern `A`, subject `\"a\"` → match (run-time `canon`, regexp.c:1130); pattern `a`, subject `\"A\"` → **no** match (the `I_CHAR` operand was never canonicalised at regexp.c:792) | [ ] |\n| 49 | js_regexec | eflags=REG_NEWLINE(2) on a prog compiled with cflags=0: pattern `^b`, subject `\"a\\nb\"` → match; multiline can be switched on per-exec without recompiling (regexp.c:1239, 1179) | [ ] |\n| 50 | js_regexec | eflags=REG_ICASE\\|REG_NEWLINE\\|REG_NOTBOL(7) all at once, pattern `^b$`, cflags=0, subject `\"a\\nB\"` → match | [ ] |\n| 51 | js_regexec | `sub == NULL`: pattern `(a)(b)`, cflags=0, eflags=0, subject `\"ab\"` → the internal `scratch` Resub is used and captures are discarded (regexp.c:1229-1233); return value still 0 | [ ] |\n| 52 | js_regexec | same `Reprog` reused across consecutive calls with different subjects/eflags — all 16 `sub[]` slots are re-cleared each call and `sub->nsub` is re-stamped from `prog->nsub` (regexp.c:1235-1237) | [ ] |\n\n## D. Pattern shapes — literals, `.`, and the top-level prologue\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 53 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | single literal rune: pattern `a`, cflags=0, eflags=0; subject `\"a\"` → match; subject `\"b\"` → no match. `L_CHAR` → `P_CHAR` → `I_CHAR` (regexp.c:440, 520-525, 790-793) | [ ] |\n| 54 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | literal concatenation (right-leaning `P_CA