{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UMmJTKEp3WQzzsPzyTZB5b","type":"tool_result","content":"31:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n36:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n47:| 11 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | `.` and the rune-level `isnewline`: pattern `a.b`, cflags=0, eflags=0; subject `\"a\\u2028b\"` (bytes E2 80 A8) → **no** match, because `I_ANY` decodes the full rune and `isnewline` rejects U+2028 (regexp.c:1120-1125, 1019-1022); subject `\"axb\"` → match |\n54:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n87:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n103:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n114:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n142:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n156:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n166:| 100 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | `\\uHHHH`: pattern `\\u00e9` (six source characters), cflags=0, eflags=0; subject `\"\\xc3\\xa9\"` (UTF-8 é) → match; subject `\"e\"` → no match (regexp.c:151-162) |\n167:| 101 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | `\\u0000` → folded to the quoted digit `'0'` and then to NUL by `lex` (regexp.c:158-161 + 400), exactly like `\\x00`; pattern `\\u0000`, cflags=0, eflags=0, subject `\"0\"` → no match, subject `\"\"` → no match |\n176:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n181:| 110 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | back-reference to a group that exists in the pattern but is unset at run time: pattern `(?:(a)\\|b)\\1`, cflags=0, eflags=0; subject `\"b\"` → match, because the unset slot has `sp == ep == NULL` so the replay length is 0 and the `if (i > 0)` guard skips the advance (regexp.c:1161, 1169-1170); subject `\"aa\"` → match (slot set to `\"a\"`); subject `\"a\"` → no match |\n188:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n211:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n234:| 153 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | deeply nested groups plus quantifiers, to exercise `count()`'s multiplicative sizing: pattern `((((a{2}){2}){2}){2})`, cflags=0, eflags=0; subject = 16 `a`s → match; subject = 15 `a`s → no match (regexp.c:657-678, 949-951) |\n239:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n252:| 166 | js_regexec | U+2028 is **not** a line terminator for `^`/`$` even with cflags=REG_NEWLINE, because `I_BOL`/`I_EOL` inspect a single `char` (`sp[-1]` / `*sp`) rather than a decoded rune: pattern `b$`, eflags=0, subject `\"b\\u2028c\"` → no match; subject `\"b\\nc\"` → match (regexp.c:1180, 1192 vs 1019-1022) |\n263:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n267:| 176 | js_regcomp + js_regexec | 15 groups where only some participate: pattern `(?:(a)\\|(b))(c)(d)(e)(f)(g)(h)(i)(j)(k)(l)(m)(n)(o)` (15 capturing groups, one non-capturing wrapper), cflags=0, eflags=0; subject `\"bcdefghijklmno\"` → match with sub[1] empty (`\"\"`) and sub[2] == `\"b\"`; subject `\"cdefghijklmno\"` → no match |\n274:|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Uk1rKJqkmq4n94NL8zq5zM","session_id":"365846c7-7961-47ff-8218-f2422469d650","uuid":"57384382-e81b-4659-897f-9c9d70d3edf3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:52:09.142Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"CONFIGS part 2: regexp"}
