`js_rot(J, 2)`, `js_rot(J, 4)` (used by `Ap_reduce`, jsarray.c:774-775), `js_rot(J, n+1)` / `js_rot(J, n+3)` from `js_construct` with `n = 0` and `n = 3` (jsrun.c:1350, 1373, 1377). | [ ] |\n| 116 | `js_dup`, `js_dup2`, `js_rot2`, `js_rot3`, `js_rot4`, `js_rot2pop1`, `js_rot3pop2` | each on a stack with exactly the minimum required depth and with extra slots below; `js_dup2` also near `JS_STACKSIZE` (`CHECKSTACK(2)`, jsrun.c:449-455) (jsrun.c:442-496). | [ ] |\n| 117 | `js_type`, `js_typeof` | call both with `idx = 0`, `-1`, and an out-of-range index for each of the 8 `js_Type` tags, plus `JS_TOBJECT` holding `JS_CFUNCTION`/`JS_CCFUNCTION` (→ `JS_ISFUNCTION`/`\"function\"`) and `JS_CSCRIPT` (→ `JS_ISOBJECT`/`\"object\"` — note `js_iscallable` is still true) (jsrun.c:280-316, 244-252). | [ ] |\n| 118 | `js_isdefined`, `js_isundefined`, `js_isnull`, `js_isboolean`, `js_isnumber`, `js_isstring`, `js_isprimitive`, `js_isobject`, `js_iscoercible`, `js_iscallable`, `js_isarray`, `js_isregexp`, `js_iserror`, `js_isuserdata` | matrix: each predicate × {undefined, null, true, 0, \"\", shrstr, litstr, memstr, plain object, array, function, cfunction, script, regexp, error, userdata, date} at `idx = -1` and at a positive index (jsrun.c:234-278). | [ ] |\n| 119 | `js_isnumberobject`, `js_isstringobject`, `js_isbooleanobject`, `js_isdateobject` | `new Number(1)`, `1`, `new String(\"\")`, `\"\"`, `new Boolean(0)`, `false`, `new Date()`, `0` — each predicate at `idx = -1` and `idx = 1` (json.c:4-22). | [ ] |\n| 120 | `js_toboolean`, `js_tonumber`, `js_tostring`, `js_tointeger`, `js_toint32`, `js_touint32`, `js_toint16`, `js_touint16` | each conversion at `idx = 0`, `idx = 1`, `idx = -1`, and an out-of-range index (→ undefined semantics) with an object argument whose `valueOf`/`toString` throws (jsrun.c:318-356). | [ ] |\n| 121 | `js_trystring`, `js_trynumber`, `js_tryinteger`, `js_tryboolean` | success path (returns the converted value) vs a value whose `valueOf` throws (returns the supplied `error` default and pops 1) vs `J->trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` (jsstate.c:47-109). | [ ] |\n| 122 | `js_getproperty`, `js_setproperty`, `js_hasproperty`, `js_delproperty`, `js_defproperty`, `js_defaccessor` | each with `idx = 0`, `idx = 1`, `idx = -1`, `idx = -2`, `idx = -3` (note `js_defaccessor` reads its two functions at `-2`/`-1` and pops 2, so the target index must account for them — jsrun.c:1026-1030), on an object receiver and on a primitive receiver (`transient`, `js_toobject` mutates the slot). | [ ] |\n| 123 | `js_getindex`, `js_setindex`, `js_hasindex`, `js_delindex` | `i = 0`, `i = 1`, `i = -1` (negative index ⇒ `js_itoa` yields `\"-1\"`, a normal property name, not an array index — jsrun.c:651-662, 803-811, 925-933), `i = INT_MAX`; receiver = simple array, unflattened array, `JS_CSTRING`, plain object, primitive string. | [ ] |\n| 124 | `js_getlength`, `js_setlength` | `js_getlength(J, 0)`, `js_getlength(J, -1)` on `[]`, `[1,2,3]`, `{length:\"3\"}`, `{length:NaN}` (→ 0 via `js_tointeger`), `{}` (no `length` → 0); `js_setlength(J, -1, 5)` and `js_setlength(J, 0, 0)` (note the `idx < 0 ? idx - 1 : idx` adjustment after the push, jsarray.c:16-20). | [ ] |\n| 125 | `js_getregistry`, `js_setregistry`, `js_delregistry`, `js_ref`, `js_unref` | `js_ref` for each value shape: undefined → `\"_Undefined\"`, null → `\"_Null\"`, true/false → `\"_True\"`/`\"_False\"`, object → `\"%p\"` interned, and a primitive number/string → the monotonically increasing `J->nextref` counter (jsrun.c:937-959). Then `js_getregistry` for a present and an absent name, `js_setregistry`, `js_delregistry`, `js_unref`. | [ ] |\n| 126 | `js_call`, `js_construct` | `js_call(J, -1)` → RangeError `\"number of arguments cannot be negative\"`; `js_call` on a non-callable → TypeError `\"<typeof> is not callable\"`; `n = 0`, `n = 1`, `n = 10`; callee = lightweight JS function (`jsR_calllwfunction`, extra args popped, missing locals padded, jsrun.c:1171-1192), non-lightweight JS function (`j