{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vvchise5sg2qz7jbbbtebvzatnnixxi3ztq6xk74tszjj7bciz6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/ERRORS.md` is written.\n\n## Verification numbers\n\n- `wc -l ERRORS.md` → **607**\n- `grep -c '^|' ERRORS.md` → **499** (includes the 20-row limit-constants table in the Legend plus the per-section table headers/separators)\n- Numbered error rows (`grep -cE '^\\| [0-9]+ \\|'`) → **445**, numbered 1..445 with no gaps or duplicates (verified programmatically)\n\n## Structure\n\n`## Legend` documents the conventions I verified in the source, then 16 sections, all sharing one continuous numbering:\n\n1. `js_regcomp`/`js_regcompx` compile rejections (rows 1-35)\n2. `js_regexec`/`js_regfree`/`js_regfreex` (36-45)\n3. `jsU_*` UTF-8/Unicode (46-68)\n4. `js_strtod`/`js_grisu2`/`js_fmtexp`/`js_strtol`/`js_itoa`/`js_stringtofloat`/`jsV_*` numerics (69-109)\n5. `jsY_ishex`/`jsY_tohex`/`jsY_iswhite`/`jsY_isnewline`/`jsY_findword`/`jsY_tokenstring` (110-118)\n6. `js_runeat`/`js_utflen`/`js_utfptrtoidx`/`js_isarrayindex` (119-131)\n7. Public stack API overflow/underflow/index (132-153)\n8. Public coercions that throw (154-168)\n9. Call/try/limit machinery (169-194)\n10. `js_newstate`/`js_dostring`/`js_ploadstring`/`try`-converters (195-214)\n11. Property access + array limits (215-250)\n12. Lexer (251-276)\n13. Parser (277-286)\n14. Compiler (287-319)\n15. RegExp built-ins (320-334)\n16. Remaining built-ins: String/Array/Object/Number/Boolean/Date/Function/JSON/URI/Math (335-445)\n\n## Key findings worth flagging\n\n- **The prompt's guessed constant names don't exist.** The real ones are `REG_MAXPROG` (32768), `REG_MAXREC` (4096), `REG_MAXSPAN` (64 → 32 ranges per class), `REG_MAXCLASS` (128), `REPINF` (255), `REG_MAXSUB` (16), plus `JS_STACKSIZE` 4096, `JS_ENVLIMIT` 1024, `JS_TRYLIMIT` 64, `JS_ARRAYLIMIT` 1<<26, `JS_ASTLIMIT` 400, `JS_STRLIMIT` 1<<28. There is no `MAXPROG`/`MAXSUB`/`MAXREP`/`MAXCLASS`/`JS_GCLIMIT`.\n- **`regexec` returns 1 for no-match, 0 for match, and additionally `-1`** for `REG_MAXREC` recursion overflow — a third value the task description didn't anticipate. All callers check `result < 0` and raise `Error \"regexec failed\"`.\n- **Invalid stack indices are not errors.** `stackidx()` silently returns a static `undefined`, so differential tests on `js_type`/`js_typeof`/`js_is*` with wild indices must expect `JS_ISUNDEFINED`/`\"undefined\"`, not a throw. Only the object-requiring paths then surface `TypeError \"cannot convert undefined to object\"`.\n- **Several public functions have no safety checks at all** and are UB-on-misuse rather than error-returning — worth marking as \"not differentially testable\": `js_rot2/3/4`, `js_rot2pop1/3pop2`, `js_rot`, `js_dup` (no underflow check); `js_pop` with negative `n`; `js_pushlstring` with negative `n` (the `while (n--)` overruns); `js_stringtofloat` unconditionally writes `*ep` with no NULL check.\n- **9 `assert()`s total**: `jsdtoa.c:386,387`, `jsstate.c:191,192`, `jsrun.c:673,674,678`, `jsproperty.c:325`. (`regexp.c:717` is only an assert mentioned in a comment.)\n- **One unchecked failure in the source**: `jsbuiltin.c:205` calls `js_regcompx(..., \"(?:)\", 0, NULL)` for `RegExp.prototype` and never checks for `NULL`.\n- I corrected ~39 line citations after cross-checking each against the file; every `file.c:NNN` in the table was verified by direct read or grep."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":236269,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":751,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013JRxv6vcd2oVDoa654wxRB","session_id":"365846c7-7961-47ff-8218-f2422469d650","uuid":"5ee9db67-d2f6-42be-bf88-769b5812afb9","timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:52:26.404Z","subagen