{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0124THAhZhSdXPMRqGqkpfD5","type":"tool_result","content":"## A. State construction, allocator, limits, reporting, context\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 482 | `js_newstate` | `js_newstate(NULL, NULL, 0)` — default allocator (`js_defaultalloc` = realloc/free, jsstate.c:15-22), `actx = NULL`, non-strict: `J->strict == J->default_strict == 0` (jsstate.c:194-205). | [ ] |\n| 483 | `js_newstate` | `js_newstate(NULL, NULL, JS_STRICT)` i.e. flags==1 — sets `J->strict = J->default_strict = 1` (jsstate.c:204-205); all of section B then takes the strict branch by default. | [ ] |\n| 484 | `js_newstate`, `js_malloc`, `js_free` | custom allocator: `js_newstate(myalloc, &myctx, 0)` with `myalloc(memctx,ptr,size)` honoring `size==0` as free; `J->actx = &myctx`, every `js_malloc/js_realloc/js_free` routes through it (jsrun.c:52-92) and `js_regcompx(J->alloc, J->actx, ...)` too (jsbuiltin.c:205). | [ ] |\n| 485 | `js_newstate` | allocator that returns NULL for the first `sizeof(js_State)` request → `js_newstate` returns NULL without touching anything (jsstate.c:197-199). | [ ] |\n| 486 | `js_newstate` | allocator that succeeds for `js_State` but returns NULL for the `JS_STACKSIZE*16` stack allocation → J is freed via `alloc(actx,J,0)` and NULL returned (jsstate.c:214-218). | [ ] |\n| 487 | `js_newstate`, `js_freestate` | allocator that throws/fails during `jsB_init` so the `js_try(J)` at jsstate.c:224 fires → `js_freestate(J)` then NULL. | [ ] |\n| 488 | `js_freestate` | `js_freestate(NULL)` — early return (jsgc.c:267-268). | [ ] |\n| 489 | `js_freestate` | after `js_dostring(J, \"var a=[1,2,3], r=/x/g, u={};\")`: frees envs, funs, objs (incl. regexp prog + CSTRING heap string + flat array), interned strings, lexbuf, stack, J (jsgc.c:260-284). | [ ] |\n| 490 | `js_setlimit` | `js_setlimit(J, 0, 0)` — both counters disabled: `J->runlimit > 0` false (jsrun.c:1602) and `J->memlimit > 0` false (jsrun.c:55, 68) ⇒ unlimited. | [ ] |\n| 491 | `js_setlimit`, `jsR_run` | `js_setlimit(J, 100000, 0)` then `js_dostring(J, \"while(1);\")` — runlimit decrements once per bytecode dispatch, throws `\"script ran too long\"` when it reaches 1 (jsrun.c:38-44, 1602-1606). | [ ] |\n| 492 | `js_setlimit`, `jsR_run` | `js_setlimit(J, 1, 0)` then any script — throws on the very first instruction (jsrun.c:1603). | [ ] |\n| 493 | `js_setlimit`, `js_malloc` | `js_setlimit(J, 0, 4096)` then `js_dostring(J, \"var s='x'; while(1) s+=s;\")` — memlimit is decremented per allocation and never credited back on free (jsrun.c:55-59, 88-92 `TODO`), so `\"out of memory\"` is thrown; single allocation `size >= memlimit` also throws (jsrun.c:56). | [ ] |\n| 494 | `js_setlimit`, `js_realloc` | `js_setlimit(J, 0, 64)` then `js_pushstring(J, <65-byte string>)` — `js_realloc` path with `size >= J->memlimit` (jsrun.c:70-71). | [ ] |\n| 495 | `js_setlimit` | `js_setlimit(J, -1, -1)` — negative values behave as unlimited (both checks are `> 0`, jsrun.c:1602, 55). | [ ] |\n| 496 | `js_gc` | `js_gc(J, 0)` — collect silently; also the implicit call from the interpreter loop when `J->gccounter > J->gcthresh` (jsrun.c:1608-1609). Recomputes `gccounter = remaining`, `gcthresh = remaining*5.0` (jsgc.c:249-250). | [ ] |\n| 497 | `js_gc`, `js_report` | `js_gc(J, 1)` — formats `\"garbage collected (%d%%): ... envs, funs, objs, props, strs\"` into a 256-byte buffer and calls `js_report` (jsgc.c:252-257). Run once on a fresh state (`ntot` non-zero) and once after everything is garbage. | [ ] |\n| 498 | `js_gc`, `js_newuserdata`, `js_newcfunctionx` | GC with unreachable `JS_CUSERDATA` / `JS_CCFUNCTION` objects that have non-NULL `finalize` — finalizer invoked from `jsG_freeobject` (jsgc.c:49-52). | [ ] |\n| 499 | `js_setreport`, `js_report` | `js_setreport(J, NULL)` then trigger a warning/report — `js_report` becomes a no-op (jsstate.c:166-170). | [ ] |\n| 500 | `js_setreport`, `js_report` | `js_setreport(J, mycb)` then `js_dostring(J, \"syntax error here\")` — message routed to `mycb`; contrast with the default `js_defaultreport` writing to stderr with a trailing newline (jsstate.c:24-28). | [ ] |\n| 501 | `js_atpanic`, `js_throw` | default panic: `js_throw(J)` with `J->trytop == 0` → `js_defaultpanic` reports `\"uncaught exception\"` then `abort()` (jsstate.c:30-34, jsrun.c:1479-1481). | [ ] |\n| 502 | `js_atpanic` | `old = js_atpanic(J, mypanic)` — returns the previous handler (`js_defaultpanic` on a fresh state) and installs the new one (jsstate.c:159-164); then `js_atpanic(J, NULL)` so `J->panic` is NULL and `js_throw` goes straight to `abort()` (jsrun.c:1479). | [ ] |\n| 503 | `js_setcontext`, `js_getcontext` | `js_setcontext(J, p); assert(js_getcontext(J) == p);` for `p == NULL` and `p == &blob` (jsstate.c:177-185); `J->uctx` starts NULL from the `memset` at jsstate.c:200. | [ ] |\n| 504 | `js_dostring` | `js_dostring(J, \"1+1\")` (returns 0) vs `js_dostring(J, \"throw new Error('x')\")` (reports via `js_trystring(J,-1,\"Error\")`, returns 1) (jsstate.c:139-157). | [ ] |\n| 505 | `js_dostring`, `js_ploadstring`, `js_ptry` | drive `J->trytop` to `JS_TRYLIMIT` (64) with nested `js_try`, then call `js_dostring`/`js_ploadstring`/`js_trystring`/`js_trynumber`/`js_tryinteger`/`js_tryboolean` — each takes the `js_ptry` overflow branch pushing the literal `\"exception stack overflow\"` (jsstate.c:5-13, 36-109). | [ ] |\n| 506 | `js_ploadstring`, `js_loadstring`, `js_loadeval` | `js_ploadstring(J, \"f.js\", \"func(\")` (syntax error → returns 1) vs valid source (returns 0 leaving a `JS_CSCRIPT` object). `js_loadstring` compiles with `J->default_strict` and scope `J->GE`; `js_loadeval` compiles with the *current* `J->strict` and scope `J->strict ? J->E : NULL` (jsstate.c:111-137). | [ ] |\n| 507 | `js_pcall`, `js_pconstruct` | `js_getglobal(J,\"f\"); js_pushundefined(J); js_pcall(J,0)` for an `f` that returns normally (0) and for one that throws (1, stack trimmed to just the error at `savetop`) (jsrun.c:1400-1426). | [ ] |\n| 508 | `js_savetry`, `js_savetrypc`, `js_endtry`, `js_throw` | `js_savetry` (pc = NULL) vs `js_savetrypc(J, pc)` (pc recorded, used by `OP_TRY`, jsrun.c:2027-2034); both snapshot `E, envtop, tracetop, top, bot, strict` (jsrun.c:1430-1456); `js_endtry` with `trytop == 0` → `\"endtry: exception stack underflow\"` (jsrun.c:1458-1463); `js_throw` restores all six fields (jsrun.c:1465-1478). | [ ] |\n| 509 | `js_savetry` | 64 nested `js_try` then one more → `js_trystackoverflow` (jsrun.c:14-20, 1446). | [ ] |\n| 510 | `js_trap` | `js_dostring(J, \"debugger;\")` → `OP_DEBUGGER` calls `js_trap` which dumps every stack slot (with `>` marking BOT) plus the trace (jsrun.c:1546-1563, 2068-2070). Exercise with each value shape on the stack so every `js_dumpvalue` case is hit (jsrun.c:1486-1526), including `v.u.object == J->G` → `[Global]`. | [ ] |\n| 511 | `jsS_dumpstrings`, `jsS_freestrings`, `js_intern` | fresh state: `jsS_dumpstrings(J)` with `J->strings == NULL` (empty tree, jsintern.c:108-115); then `js_intern(J,\"b\"); js_intern(J,\"a\"); js_intern(J,\"c\"); js_intern(J,\"a\")` (dedupe returns the same pointer, jsintern.c:130-137) and dump again; `jsS_freestrings` on empty vs populated (jsintern.c:124-128). | [ ] |\n| 512 | `js_intern` | `js_intern` with a string longer than `JS_STRLIMIT` → RangeError `\"invalid string length\"` (jsintern.c:46-47). | [ ] |\n| 513 | `js_putc`, `js_puts`, `js_putm` | `js_Buffer *sb = NULL; js_putc(J,&sb,'a')` (first call allocates, `m = 64`), then push >64 bytes so the `sb->n == sb->m` doubling branch fires (jsintern.c:5-18); `js_puts(J,&sb,\"\")` (no-op) vs non-empty; `js_putm(J,&sb,s,s)` (empty range) vs `js_putm(J,&sb,s,s+3)` (jsintern.c:20-30). | [ ] |\n| 514 | `js_malloc`, `js_realloc`, `js_free`, `js_strdup` | `js_strdup(J,\"\")` (1 byte) and `js_strdup(J,\"abc\")`; `js_realloc(J, NULL, 32)` (fresh alloc path) vs growing an existing block; allocator returning NULL → `\"out of memory\"` thrown (jsrun.c:52-92). | [ ] |\n\n## B. Strict-mode-dependent behaviours (one row per distinct branch on `J->strict` / `F->strict`)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 515 | `js_setvar` (OP_SETVAR) | assignment to an undeclared variable: `js_dostring(J, \"undeclared = 1;\")`. Non-strict: creates a property on `J->G`. Strict: ReferenceError `\"assignment to undeclared variable 'undeclared'\"` (jsrun.c:1132-1134). | [ ] |\n| 516 | `js_setvar` | assignment to a read-only binding: `js_dostring(J, \"NaN = 1;\")` / `\"undefined = 1;\"` (globals defined `JS_READONLY|JS_DONTENUM|JS_DONTCONF`, jsbuiltin.c:232-238). Non-strict: silent. Strict: TypeError `\"'NaN' is read-only\"` (jsrun.c:1124-1128). | [ ] |\n| 517 | `js_delvar` (OP_DELVAR/OP_DELLOCAL) | `js_dostring(J, \"var x=1; (function(){ return delete x; })()\")` — env var is `JS_DONTENUM|JS_DONTCONF` (`js_initvar`, jsrun.c:1087). Non-strict: returns false. Strict: TypeError `\"'x' is non-configurable\"` (jsrun.c:1143-1147). Note the compiler additionally rejects `delete <identifier>` in strict at compile time (row 47). | [ ] |\n| 518 | `jsR_setproperty` | write through an accessor that has only a getter: `js_dostring(J, \"var o={get a(){return 1}}; o.a = 2;\")`. Non-strict: silent no-op. Strict: TypeError `\"setting property 'a' that only has a getter\"` (jsrun.c:771-773). | [ ] |\n| 519 | `jsR_setproperty` | write to a `JS_READONLY` own/inherited data property: `js_dostring(J, \"var o={}; Object.defineProperty(o,'a',{value:1,writable:false}); o.a=2;\")`. Non-strict: silent. Strict: TypeError `\"'a' is read-only\"` (jsrun.c:774-775, 790-800). | [ ] |\n| 520 | `jsR_setproperty`, `js_setproperty` | write to a *transient* object (primitive receiver): `js_dostring(J, \"'abc'.foo = 1;\")`, or C-side `js_pushstring(J,\"abc\"); js_pushnumber(J,1); js_setproperty(J,-2,\"foo\")` (transient = `!js_isobject`, jsrun.c:1011). Non-strict: silent. Strict: TypeError `\"cannot create property 'foo' on transient object\"` (jsrun.c:780-785). | [ ] |\n| 521 | `jsR_setproperty` | write to a built-in read-only slot: `js_dostring(J, \"'abc'.length = 9;\")` (CSTRING length / index, jsrun.c:736-742) and `js_dostring(J, \"/x/.source='y';\")` (CREGEXP source/global/ignoreCase/multiline, jsrun.c:744-748) — reaches `readonly:` (jsrun.c:798-800). | [ ] |\n| 522 | `jsR_defproperty` | define a value over a `JS_READONLY` property: `js_pushnumber(J,1); js_defproperty(J, idx, \"ro\", 0)` where `ro` already has `JS_READONLY`. Non-strict: value silently dropped. Strict: TypeError `\"'ro' is read-only\"` (jsrun.c:850-855). | [ ] |\n| 523 | `jsR_defproperty`, `js_defaccessor` | install a getter and/or setter over a `JS_DONTCONF` property: `js_newcfunction(...); js_pushnull(J); js_defaccessor(J, idx, \"frozen\", 0)` after `Object.freeze`. Non-strict: silently ignored. Strict: TypeError `\"'frozen' is non-configurable\"` (jsrun.c:856-867). | [ ] |\n| 524 | `jsR_defproperty` | `throw` argument: `js_defproperty`/`js_defaccessor` pass `throw = 1`, `js_defglobal`, `js_initvar`, `OP_INITGETTER`, `OP_INITSETTER` pass `throw = 0` (jsrun.c:995, 1017, 1028, 1087, 1744, 1751). Test `js_newarray(J); js_pushnumber(J,1); js_defproperty(J,-2,\"length\",0)` — array `length` hits `readonly:` which throws when `J->strict || throw` (jsrun.c:820-822, 873-875), so it throws even in non-strict via `js_defproperty` but not via `js_defglobal`. | [ ] |\n| 525 | `jsR_delproperty` | delete a `JS_DONTCONF` property or a built-in slot: `js_dostring(J, \"var o={}; Object.seal(o); delete o.a;\")`, `\"delete [].length\"`, `\"delete 'ab'[0]\"`, `\"delete /x/.lastIndex\"` (jsrun.c:883-909, 911-916). Non-strict: returns false. Strict: TypeError `\"'...' is non-configurable\"` (jsrun.c:919-922). | [ ] |\n| 526 | `jsV_setproperty` | add a property to a non-extensible object: `js_dostring(J, \"var o=Object.preventExtensions({}); o.a=1;\")`. Non-strict: returns NULL, silently ignored. Strict: TypeError `\"object is non-extensible\"` (jsproperty.c:225-230). | [ ] |\n| 527 | `jsR_run` / `OP_THIS` | `this` coercion: `js_dostring(J, \"function f(){ return typeof this; } f();\")`. Non-strict: `this` is not coercible ⇒ replaced by the global object (`js_pushglobal`). Strict: the raw (undefined) value is copied (jsrun.c:1651-1660). | [ ] |\n| 528 | `jsR_callfunction`, `js_newarguments` | `arguments.callee`: `js_dostring(J, \"function f(){ return arguments.callee; } f();\")`. Non-strict: `callee` defined `JS_DONTENUM`. Strict: not defined at all (jsrun.c:1203-1217). `length` is always defined. | [ ] |\n| 529 | `jsV_toprimitive` | object with no callable `toString`/`valueOf`: `js_dostring(J, \"var o = Object.create(null); '' + o;\")`. Non-strict: yields the literal string `\"[object]\"`. Strict: TypeError `\"cannot convert object to primitive\"` (jsvalue.c:117-149). | [ ] |\n| 530 | `jsC_compilescript`, `cfunbody` | `'use strict'` directive prologue: `js_dostring(J, \"'use strict'; undeclared = 1;\")` and the function-level form `\"function f(){ 'use strict'; undeclared=1; } f();\"` — only checked when the *first* statement of the body is a string literal equal to `use strict` (jscompile.c:1382-1385). Also test a non-first `'use strict'` (no effect). | [ ] |\n| 531 | `checkfutureword` | strict future reserved words `implements interface let package private protected public static yield` (jscompile.c:35-38): `js_dostring(J, \"var yield = 1;\")` — non-strict OK, strict SyntaxError `\"'yield' is a strict mode future reserved word\"` (jscompile.c:44-46). Contrast the always-rejected `futurewords` list `class const enum export extends import super` (jscompile.c:31-33, 42-43). | [ ] |\n| 532 | `addlocal` | `arguments` as a declared name: `js_dostring(J, \"function f(){ var arguments; }\")` — strict SyntaxError `\"redefining 'arguments' is not allowed in strict mode\"` (jscompile.c:112-114); non-strict accepted. | [ ] |\n| 533 | `addlocal` | `eval` as a declared name: `js_dostring(J, \"function f(eval){}\")` — strict: `\"redefining 'eval' is not allowed in strict mode\"`; non-strict: EvalError `\"invalid use of 'eval'\"` (jscompile.c:112-119) — *both* reject, with different error classes. | [ ] |\n| 534 | `addlocal` | duplicate formal parameter: `js_dostring(J, \"function f(a,a){}\")` — strict SyntaxError `\"duplicate formal parameter 'a'\"`; non-strict accepted (jscompile.c:121-131). Also `reuse=1` path from `cfunbody` binding a named function expression (jscompile.c:1391-1398). | [ ] |\n| 535 | `emitlocal` | assigning to `arguments` / `eval`: `js_dostring(J, \"function f(){ arguments = 1; }\")` and `\"function f(){ eval = 1; }\")` — strict SyntaxError `\"'arguments' is read-only in strict mode\"` / `\"'eval' is read-only in strict mode\"` (jscompile.c:202-207). Note `eval` as an identifier at all triggers EvalError at jscompile.c:208-209. | [ ] |\n| 536 | `cobject`, `checkdup` | duplicate property in an object literal: `js_dostring(J, \"var o = {a:1, a:2};\")` and the numeric-key variant `\"({1:1, 1.0:2})\"` (keys normalized via `jsV_numbertostring`, jscompile.c:297-318) — strict SyntaxError `\"duplicate property 'a' in object literal\"`; non-strict accepted (jscompile.c:339-340). | [ ] |\n| 537 | `cdelete` | `delete` on an unqualified name: `js_dostring(J, \"var x; delete x;\")` — strict SyntaxError `\"delete on an unqualified name is not allowed in strict mode\"` (jscompile.c:506-508); non-strict compiles to `OP_DELLOCAL`/`OP_DELVAR`. | [ ] |\n| 538 | `ctrycatch`, `ctrycatchfinally` | catch parameter named `arguments`/`eval`: `js_dostring(J, \"try{}catch(eval){}\")` and the `try/catch/finally` form — strict SyntaxError (jscompile.c:957-963 and 989-995). Note `checkfutureword` is called unconditionally in `ctrycatch` but only inside the `if (F->strict)` block in `ctrycatchfinally` — a real behavioural difference between the two shapes. | [ ] |\n| 539 | `cstm` / `STM_WITH` | `js_dostring(J, \"with({a:1}) { a; }\")` — non-strict: compiles to `OP_WITH`/`OP_ENDWITH` and forces `F->lightweight = 0`; strict: SyntaxError `\"'with' statements are not allowed in strict mode\"` (jscompile.c:1263-1273). | [ ] |\n| 540 | `lexnumber` | legacy octal literal `js_dostring(J, \"010\")` — **not** strict-dependent in this build: always SyntaxError `\"number with leading zero\"` (jslex.c:311-312/350-351). Also `\"0x10\"` (accepted) and `\"1abc\"` → `\"number with letter suffix\"`. | [ ] |\n| 541 | `jsR_run`, `js_savetry`, `js_throw` | strict flag is per-function and save/restored: `jsR_run` sets `J->strict = F->strict` on entry and restores `savestrict` at `OP_RETURN` (jsrun.c:1594-1595, 2092-2094); `js_savetry`/`js_savetrypc` snapshot it and `js_throw` restores it (jsrun.c:1439, 1453, 1475). Test a non-strict function calling a strict one that throws, caught in the non-strict caller. | [ ] |\n| 542 | `js_loadeval`, `js_eval` (OP_EVAL) | direct `eval`: `js_dostring(J, \"eval('var q=1;'); q;\")` in a non-strict state (compiled with `J->default_strict`, scope NULL ⇒ runs in the caller's env, jsstate.c:122-124, jsrun.c:1237-1264) vs a `JS_STRICT` state (compiled strict, scope `J->E`). Also `js_eval` with a non-string on top of the stack → returns unchanged (jsrun.c:1390-1393). | [ ] |\n\n## C. Property attribute flags (`JS_READONLY=1`, `JS_DONTENUM=2`, `JS_DONTCONF=4`)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 543 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = 0` — plain writable/enumerable/configurable property; then overwrite, enumerate with `for-in`, and `delete` it (all succeed). | [ ] |\n| 544 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_READONLY (1)` — subsequent `js_setproperty`/JS assignment is dropped (jsrun.c:789-793); `delete` still works; still enumerable. | [ ] |\n| 545 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_DONTENUM (2)` — hidden from `for-in` (`jsV_getenumproperty`/`itwalk`, jsproperty.c:210-219, 252-264), from `Object.keys` (jsobject.c:352-363) and from `propertyIsEnumerable` (jsobject.c:100-106), but still visible to `Object.getOwnPropertyNames` (jsobject.c:157-166) and `hasOwnProperty`. | [ ] |\n| 546 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_DONTCONF (4)` — `delete` fails (jsrun.c:913-914) and getter/setter installation is refused (jsrun.c:857, 863); value writes still allowed. | [ ] |\n| 547 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_READONLY|JS_DONTENUM (3)`. | [ ] |\n| 548 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_READONLY|JS_DONTCONF (5)` — the \"frozen property\" shape (`O_freeze_walk`, jsobject.c:475-482; `O_isFrozen` requires exactly these two, jsobject.c:501-514). | [ ] |\n| 549 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_DONTENUM|JS_DONTCONF (6)` — the shape used by `js_initvar` for function-scope variables (jsrun.c:1087) and by `\"prototype\"` on functions (jsvalue.c:470). | [ ] |\n| 550 | `js_defproperty` | `atts = JS_READONLY|JS_DONTENUM|JS_DONTCONF (7)` — the shape used for `function.length` (jsvalue.c:464, 505, 531), `jsB_propn` numeric constants (jsbuiltin.c:21), `NaN`/`Infinity`/`undefined` globals (jsbuiltin.c:232-238), `Error.prototype.stack` accessor (jserror.c:121) and `Fp_bind`'s `__TargetFunction__`/`__BoundThis__`/`__BoundArguments__` (jsfunction.c:200-212). | [ ] |\n| 551 | `js_defproperty` | attributes are **accumulated, never cleared**: `js_defproperty(idx,\"a\",JS_READONLY)` then `js_defproperty(idx,\"a\",0)` — `ref->atts |= atts` (jsrun.c:868) so `a` stays read-only. Verify with `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor`. | [ ] |\n| 552 | `js_defglobal`, `js_delglobal`, `js_getglobal`, `js_setglobal` | `js_pushnumber(J,1); js_defglobal(J,\"g\",JS_DONTENUM)` (throw=0 path, jsrun.c:993-997) then `js_getglobal`, `js_setglobal`, `js_delglobal`; repeat with `atts = JS_READONLY|JS_DONTCONF` and observe `js_setglobal`/`js_delglobal` in strict vs non-strict. | [ ] |\n| 553 | `js_defaccessor` | `js_newcfunction(J,getter,\"g\",0); js_newcfunction(J,setter,\"s\",1); js_defaccessor(J, idx, \"p\", 0)` — both getter and setter installed; then the getter-only variant (`js_pushnull` for the setter, as in jserror.c:119-121) and the setter-only variant (`js_pushundefined` for the getter). `jsR_tofunction` accepts undefined/null (→NULL) and functions, else TypeError `\"not a function\"` (jsrun.c:385-394, 1026-1030). | [ ] |\n| 554 | `js_defaccessor`, `jsR_hasproperty`, `jsR_setproperty` | accessor invocation shapes: read through a getter (`js_call(J,0)` with the object as `this`, jsrun.c:632-636), write through a setter (`js_call(J,1)`, jsrun.c:763-769), and read/write an accessor found on the **prototype** rather than the object itself (`jsV_getpropertyx` `own` flag, jsproperty.c:186-197, jsrun.c:761, 780). | [ ] |\n| 555 | `js_defaccessor`, `js_setvar`, `js_hasvar` | accessor on an *environment* record (via `with`): `js_dostring(J, \"var o={get a(){return 1}, set a(v){}}; with(o){ a; a=2; }\")` — exercises the getter/setter branches in `js_hasvar` (jsrun.c:1096-1101) and `js_setvar` (jsrun.c:1116-1122). | [ ] |\n| 556 | `O_getOwnPropertyDescriptor`, `ToPropertyDescriptor` | `Object.defineProperty(o,'a',{value:1,writable:true,enumerable:true,configurable:true})`, then each of the 8 boolean combinations, then `{get:f}`, `{set:f}`, `{get:f,set:g}`, and the error shape `{value:1,get:f}` → TypeError `\"value/writable and get/set attributes are exclusive\"` (jsobject.c:222-273); read back with `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor` (jsobject.c:120-155, including the `undefined` result for a missing property). | [ ] |\n\n## D. Value / data shapes\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 557 | `js_pushundefined`, `js_type`, `js_typeof`, `jsV_toboolean/tonumber/tostring/toobject` | `undefined`: `js_type` → `JS_ISUNDEFINED`,