{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vnptgozada27egfc7ifqwy6systgz4nbyzl33c2t4ay2qsx2khqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01CDfm4XmZDzwhdzPjH3KgKt","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write valid-path JS corpora","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno\n\nYou are writing TEST CORPORA for a C-to-Rust differential test of the MuJS JavaScript engine.\nRead ONLY `c_src/` (NEVER modify it) plus `translation/CONFIGS.md` for guidance.\n\nCreate these SIX files, each a plain-text corpus of JavaScript snippets:\n\n1. `translation/tests/corpus/language.txt`                 (>= 200 lines)\n2. `translation/tests/corpus/builtins_object_function.txt` (>= 150 lines)\n3. `translation/tests/corpus/builtins_array.txt`           (>= 150 lines)\n4. `translation/tests/corpus/builtins_string.txt`          (>= 180 lines)\n5. `translation/tests/corpus/builtins_number_math.txt`     (>= 180 lines)\n6. `translation/tests/corpus/strict_mode.txt`              (>= 70 lines)\n\nSTRICT FILE FORMAT (a test harness parses these; deviating breaks the build):\n- ONE self-contained JavaScript snippet per line. NO snippet may span multiple lines.\n- Lines starting with `#` are comments; blank lines are ignored. Use comments to group.\n- To embed a newline inside a snippet, write the two characters backslash + n (`\\n`);\n  the harness converts `\\n` -> newline and `\\t` -> tab before compiling.\n  So a JS string containing a literal newline is written `'a\\nb'` and a multi-statement\n  snippet can be written `var a=1;\\nvar b=2;\\na+b`.\n- CRITICAL: because `\\n` is rewritten, a JS regex or string that needs a LITERAL\n  backslash-n sequence must be avoided; prefer `String.fromCharCode(10)` instead.\n- Each snippet's VALUE MATTERS: the harness compares the stringified result of the\n  snippet between the C and Rust builds. So prefer snippets that EVALUATE TO a\n  value (an expression, or statements ending in an expression). Wrap multi-statement\n  logic in an IIFE returning a value, e.g.\n  `(function(){var a=[1,2]; a.push(3); return a.join('|')})()`\n- These are VALID-PATH snippets: they should normally NOT throw. (A few that throw\n  are fine, since the error message is compared too, but the focus is valid paths.)\n- Every snippet is run TWICE by the harness: once with flags=0 and once with\n  flags=JS_STRICT. You do NOT need to add 'use strict' yourself except in\n  strict_mode.txt where you are specifically testing the directive.\n\nCONTENT REQUIREMENTS (derive the specific edge cases from the C source):\n\n`language.txt` — core language semantics: all literal forms (numbers incl. hex and\n  decimals and exponents, strings with every escape `\\\\' \\\\\" \\\\\\\\ \\\\b \\\\f \\\\r \\\\t \\\\v \\\\0\n  \\\\xHH \\\\uHHHH` and line continuations, `true/false/null/undefined`, array literals\n  with elisions `[1,,3]` and trailing commas, object literals incl. numeric and string\n  keys, getters/setters in literals), operator precedence and associativity, all\n  assignment operators (`+= -= *= /= %= <<= >>= >>>= &= |= ^=`), comma operator,\n  `in`, `instanceof`, `delete`, `void`, `typeof`, ternary, short-circuit evaluation\n  order, `++`/`--` prefix and postfix on variables and properties and array elements,\n  string vs numeric `+`, ToPrimitive ordering, `==` coercion table, `===`,\n  relational comparison of strings vs numbers, bitwise ops at the 2^31/2^32\n  boundaries, `>>>` vs `>>`, all statements (`if/else`, `while`, `do-while`, `for`,\n  `for-in`, `switch` with fallthrough and default in the middle, `break`/`continue`\n  with and without labels, `try/catch/finally` in all combinations, `throw`,\n  `with`, `var` hoisting, function declaration hoisting, named function expressions,\n  `arguments` object aliasing and `.length` and `.callee`, `this` binding in all\n  call forms, `new` with and without a returned object, prototype chains,\n  automatic semicolon insertion cases, `debugger`).\n\n`builtins_object_function.txt` — `Object` (constructor called as function and with\n  `new`, `Object.keys/getOwnPropertyNames/getPrototypeOf/create/defineProperty/\n  defineProperties/getOwnPropertyDescriptor/seal/freeze/isSealed/isFrozen/\n  preventExtensions/isExtensible`), `Object.prototype`\n  (`toString/valueOf/hasOwnProperty/isPrototypeOf/propertyIsEnumerable/toLocaleString`),\n  `Function.prototype` (`toString/apply/call/bind` incl. bound-function `length`,\n  bound constructors, `apply` with array-likes and with 0/1/many args), and\n  the global functions `eval/parseInt/parseFloat/isNaN/isFinite/\n  encodeURI/encodeURIComponent/decodeURI/decodeURIComponent/escape/unescape`.\n  Include the exact edge cases the C branches on (read `jsbuiltin.c`, `jsobject.c`,\n  `jsfunction.c`): parseInt radix 0/2/8/10/16/36, leading `0x`, whitespace, signs;\n  URI encoding of ASCII vs 2-byte vs 3-byte vs surrogate-pair characters.\n\n`builtins_array.txt` — `Array` (as function and with `new`, `new Array(n)` for\n  n=0/1/5, `new Array(1,2,3)`, `Array.isArray`), and every `Array.prototype`\n  method in `jsarray.c` (`toString join concat pop push reverse shift slice sort\n  splice unshift indexOf lastIndexOf every some forEach map filter reduce\n  reduceRight`) with edge shapes: empty array, one element, holes/sparse,\n  negative and out-of-range start/end/deleteCount, fractional args, missing args,\n  extra args, `length` mutation, non-array `this` via `call`, custom sort\n  comparators (including inconsistent ones), nested arrays in `join`/`toString`,\n  and `length` at the 2^32-1 boundary.\n\n`builtins_string.txt` — `String` (as function and with `new`, `String.fromCharCode`\n  with 0/1/many args and out-of-range and fractional codes), and every\n  `String.prototype` method in `jsstring.c` (`toString valueOf charAt charCodeAt\n  concat indexOf lastIndexOf localeCompare match replace search slice split\n  substring substr toLowerCase toUpperCase toLocaleLowerCase toLocaleUpperCase\n  trim`) with edge shapes: empty string, negative / fractional / NaN / Infinity /\n  missing / extra index args, multi-byte UTF-8 and surrogate pairs, `replace`\n  with a string containing `$$ $& $\\` $' $1`..`$9` patterns, `replace` with a\n  function replacement, `split` with a string separator / regexp separator /\n  empty separator / limit argument, `match` with and without the `g` flag,\n  case conversion of characters with special Unicode mappings (e.g. `ß`,\n  `İ`, `ı`, `ẞ`, `ﬀ`) and of astral characters.\n\n`builtins_number_math.txt` — `Number` (as function and with `new`, the constants\n  `MAX_VALUE MIN_VALUE NaN POSITIVE_INFINITY NEGATIVE_INFINITY`) and\n  `Number.prototype` (`toString` with radix 2..36, `toFixed` 0..20,\n  `toExponential` 0..20, `toPrecision` 1..21, `valueOf`, `toLocaleString`) over\n  0, -0, tiny, huge, NaN, +/-Infinity, exact integers, values needing 17 digits,\n  and the 1e21 / 1e-7 notation fence-posts; plus every `Math` function in\n  `jsmath.c` (`abs acos asin atan atan2 ceil cos exp floor log max min pow\n  random round sin sqrt tan` and the constants `E LN10 LN2 LOG10E LOG2E PI\n  SQRT1_2 SQRT2`) over 0, -0, NaN, +/-Infinity, negatives, values out of domain\n  (e.g. `Math.sqrt(-1)`, `Math.acos(2)`, `Math.log(-1)`), `Math.max()`/`Math.min()`\n  with 0/1/many args and with NaN present, `Math.pow` special cases\n  (`pow(0,0) pow(1,Infinity) pow(-1,Infinity) pow(NaN,0)`), and `Math.round`\n  half-way and negative-zero cases. IMPORTANT: `Math.random` is\n  nondeterministic -- only use it in snippets whose value does not depend on it\n  (e.g. `typeof Math.random()`, `Math.random()>=0 && Math.random()<1`).\n\n`strict_mode.txt` — one snippet per distinct strict-mode-dependent branch you can\n  find by grepping `J->strict` and `F->strict` in the C source (see also\n  CONFIGS.md section B). Each snippet must be written so that running it in\n  non-strict mode and in strict mode gives DIFFERENT observable results (a value\n  vs a specific error), because the harness runs each snippet in both modes and\n  compares. Include the `'use strict'` directive forms (both program-level and\n  function-body-level, and a non-first-statement one that has no effect).\n  Wrap in try/catch where you want to observe the error message as a value,\n  e.g. `(function(){try{ undeclaredVar=1; return 'ok' }catch(e){ return e.name+': '+e.message }})()`\n\nQUALITY BAR: derive the edge cases by actually reading the corresponding C files.\nDo not just write generic JS. Every line should target a branch you saw in the source.\n\nAfter writing, verify and report for each file: `wc -l`, and the count of\nnon-comment non-blank lines. Also confirm no line contains an unescaped real newline\n(each file's line count should equal the number of snippets plus comments)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10108,"cache_read_input_tokens":264354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10108,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"365846c7-7961-47ff-8218-f2422469d650","uuid":"f6cd4073-94cb-4322-8141-1874179777dc","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:04:13.611Z"}
