{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DjcWyGz1QVDn4tDJ4wSetp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — Configuration-Surface Table (MuJS)\n2\t\n3\tThe mirror of `ERRORS.md`: every VALID configuration axis the C code branches on,\n4\tenumerated mechanically from `c_src/`. One row per meaningful combination of\n5\t(runtime options set) x (input shape) that the C treats differently.\n6\t\n7\tRows are renumbered contiguously across the three derivation parts. The `[ ]`\n8\tcolumn is checked once a differential test covering that row passes against BOTH\n9\tthe C `.so` and the Rust `.so` across randomized inputs.\n10\t\n11\tCoverage map (which test file exercises which part):\n12\t\n13\t| part | modules | test file(s) |\n14\t|---|---|---|\n15\t| P1 | utf, dtoa, number conversion, string->number, lexer helpers, string helpers | `tests/b01_utf.rs`, `tests/b02_number.rs`, `tests/b04_lexer_strhelpers.rs` |\n16\t| P2 | regexp compile + exec | `tests/b03_regexp.rs`, `tests/b06_scripts.rs` |\n17\t| P3 | state, runtime, objects, properties, builtins, compiler | `tests/b05_stackapi.rs`, `tests/b06_scripts.rs`, `tests/c07_errors.rs` |\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t# Part 1 — utf, dtoa, number conversion, lexer helpers, string helpers\n21\t\n22\t\n23\t## utf.c / utfdata.h (jsU_* rune codec + Unicode tables)\n24\t\n25\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n26\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n27\t| 1 | `jsU_chartorune` | byte seq = `C0 80` (MuJS's private overlong encoding of U+0000) → rune 0, length 2; special-cased ahead of all range logic. Contrast byte seq = `00` (real NUL, `str[1]` != 0x80) → rune 0, length 1 via `c < Tx` (utf.c:58-61 vs 67-71) | [ ] |\n28\t| 2 | `jsU_chartorune` | 1-byte class fence-posts: byte = `7F` (accepted, `c < Tx`) vs byte seq = `80 41` (bare continuation as lead: `c >= Tx` but `c < T2` → `bad`, rune 0xFFFD, length 1) (utf.c:68, 81-82, 127-129) | [ ] |\n29\t| 3 | `jsU_chartorune` | 2-byte accepts vs rejects: `C2 A2` (U+00A2) and `DF BF` (U+07FF = Rune2, top of range) → length 2; `C1 BF` (overlong for U+007F, `l <= Rune1`) and `C2 20` (bad continuation, `c1 & Testx`) → rune 0xFFFD, length 1 (utf.c:77-87) | [ ] |\n30\t| 4 | `jsU_chartorune` | 3-byte accepts vs rejects: `E2 82 AC` (U+20AC), `EF BF BF` (U+FFFF = Rune3), and `ED A0 80` — the last is a lone surrogate U+D800 and is ACCEPTED because only `l <= Rune2` is checked (no surrogate guard); rejects are `E0 80 80` (overlong) and `E2 82 20` (bad third byte, `c2 & Testx`) (utf.c:94-103) | [ ] |\n31\t| 5 | `jsU_chartorune` | 4-byte: `F0 9F 98 80` (valid U+1F600) and `F4 8F BF BF` (U+10FFFF = Runemax, accepted) vs rejects `F0 80 80 80` (`l <= Rune3`), `F4 90 80 80` (`l > Runemax`), `F0 9F 98 20` (`c3 & Testx`), and `F8 88 80 80 80` (5-byte lead, `c >= T5`, falls out of the guard to `bad`) (utf.c:109-122) | [ ] |\n32\t| 6 | `jsU_runetochar` / `jsU_runelen` | one input per output-length class: rune 0 → `C0 80` (2); 0x41 and 0x7F (`<= Rune1`) → 1; 0x80 and 0x7FF (`<= Rune2`) → 2; 0x800 and 0xFFFF (`<= Rune3`) → 3; 0x10000 and 0x10FFFF → 4; rune 0x110000 (`c > Runemax`) → silently coerced to Runeerror and emitted as the 3 bytes `EF BF BD` (utf.c:135-185, 194) | [ ] |\n33\t| 7 | `jsU_tolowerrune` / `jsU_toupperrune` / `jsU_islowerrune` / `jsU_isupperrune` | range-table (`ne=3`) hits: c = 0x41 → +32 from `ucd_tolower2` [0x41,0x5A]; c = 0x61 → -32 from `ucd_toupper2`; c = 0x23F → +10815 (large positive delta); c = 0x1E900 (last `ucd_tolower2` entry, driving the binary search to the final element) (utf.c:203-211, 222-224, 236-238, 250-270; utfdata.h:700, 751, 1380-1382) | [ ] |\n34\t| 8 | `jsU_tolowerrune` | range MISS after a successful bsearch: c = 0xD7 (bsearch returns the [0xC0,0xD6] triple but `c > p[1]`) → falls through to the `ne=2` table, then identity. Singleton (`ne=2`) exact hits: c = 0x100 (delta +1) and c = 0xA7DC (delta -42561); adjacent miss c = 0