y point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n155\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n156\t| 85 | `jsY_iswhite` | accepted: c ∈ {0x9, 0xB, 0xC, 0x20, 0xA0, 0xFEFF} (six separate `==` terms). Rejected near-misses: c ∈ {0x0, 0xA, 0xD, 0x41, 0xA1, 0x2028, 0xFEFE} (jslex.c:109-112) | [ ] |\n157\t| 86 | `jsY_isnewline` | accepted: c ∈ {0xA, 0xD, 0x2028, 0x2029}. Rejected: c ∈ {0x9, 0xB, 0xC, 0x2027, 0x202A} — note 0xA/0xD are exactly the values `jsY_iswhite` excludes (jslex.c:114-117) | [ ] |\n158\t| 87 | `jsY_ishex` | accepted: c ∈ {`'0'`, `'9'`, `'a'`, `'f'`, `'A'`, `'F'`} (both the `isdigit` and the `ishex` sub-ranges). Rejected fence-posts: c ∈ {`'/'`, `':'`, `` '`' ``, `'g'`, `'@'`, `'G'`} (jslex.c:123, 126, 144-147) | [ ] |\n159\t| 88 | `jsY_tohex` | c = `'0'`→0 and `'9'`→9 (first test); `'a'`→10 and `'f'`→15 (second); `'A'`→10 and `'F'`→15 (third); c ∈ {`'g'`, `'G'`, `'Z'`, 0} → falls through all three tests and returns 0, indistinguishable from `'0'` (callers must pre-check with `jsY_ishex`) (jslex.c:149-155) | [ ] |\n160\t| 89 | `jsY_findword` | list = `keywords`, num = 29: hits on `\"if\"` (mid), `\"break\"` (first), `\"with\"` (last), exercising both `l = m+1` and `r = m-1`; misses `\"aaa\"` (before all), `\"zzz\"` (after all), `\"brea\"` (proper prefix, `strcmp < 0`), `\"breakx\"` (`strcmp > 0`) → -1; and num = 0 → `r = -1`, loop never entered → -1 (jslex.c:81-96) | [ ] |\n161\t| 90 | `jsY_tokenstring` | token = 0 → `\"(end-of-file)\"`; token = 65 → `\"'A'\"`; token = 0x7F → `\"'\\\\x7F'\"`; token ∈ 0x80..0xFF → the table entry is a literal `0` so `if (tokenstring[token])` fails → `\"<unknown>\"`; token = TK_IDENTIFIER..TK_REGEXP (the named entries after the hole); token = TK_WITH (last entry) vs TK_WITH+1 (`>= nelem`) → `\"<unknown>\"`; token = -1 (`token >= 0` false) → `\"<unknown>\"` (jslex.c:23-72) | [ ] |\n162\t\n163\t## jslex.c — jsY_initlex / jsY_lex / jsY_lexjson\n164\t\n165\t| # | entry point(