`, `-0`, `Date` objects, `Number`/`String`/`Boolean` wrappers, objects\n  with a `toJSON` method, nested structures, sparse arrays, non-enumerable\n  properties; and the `replacer` argument as both a function and an array, and the\n  `space` argument as 0, a number 1..10, a number out of range (negative and > 10),\n  a short string, and a string longer than 10 characters.\n\n`builtins_date.txt` — VALID-PATH Date snippets. IMPORTANT: avoid anything depending\n  on the CURRENT time or the local timezone where the result could differ between\n  two runs -- prefer explicit UTC timestamps and the `getUTC*` accessors, and for\n  local-time functions only use snippets whose value is timezone-independent\n  (or note that both builds run in the same process so the TZ is identical -- local\n  time IS comparable, but `Date.now()`/`new Date()` with no args is NOT).\n  Cover: `new Date(ms)` for 0, negative, huge, NaN, and the +/-8.64e15 valid-range\n  boundary; `new Date(y,m,d,h,mi,s,ms)` with in-range and out-of-range (overflowing)\n  components and with 2..7 arguments; `new Date(string)` for the ISO forms the C\n  parses; `Date.parse`, `Date.UTC`, and every `Date.prototype` getter and setter in\n  `c_src/src/jsdate.c` (`getTime getFullYear getMonth getDate getDay getHours\n  getMinutes getSeconds getMilliseconds getTimezoneOffset` and their `getUTC*`\n  variants, plus `setTime setFullYear setMonth setDate setHours setMinutes\n  setSeconds setMilliseconds` and the `setUTC*` variants with 1..N arguments),\n  and `toString toDateString toTimeString toUTCString toISOString toJSON\n  valueOf toLocaleString toLocaleDateString toLocaleTimeString`.\n\nHOW TO VERIFY (do this before finishing — it is required):\nThe C shared library is already built at `c_src/build/libmujs.so`. Write a small\nC driver to check your corpora. For example:\n\n```bash\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno\ncat > /tmp/chk.c <<'EOF'\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include \"mujs.h\"\nstatic void rep(js_State *J, const char *m){ printf(\"  ERR %s\\n\", m); }\nint main(int argc, char **argv){\n  char line[65536]; FILE *f = fopen(argv[1], \"r\"); int n=0, bad=0;\n  while (fgets(line, sizeof line, f)) {\n    int L = strlen(line); while (L && (line[L-1]=='\\n'||line[L-1]=='\\r')) line[--L]=0;\n    if (!L || line[0]=='#') continue;\n    /* expand \\n and \\t like the Rust harness does */\n    char src[65536]; int o=0;\n    for (int i=0;i<L;i++){ if(line[i]=='\\\\'&&line[i+1]=='n'){src[o++]='\\n';i++;}\n      else if(line[i]=='\\\\'&&line[i+1]=='t'){src[o++]='\\t';i++;} else src[o++]=line[i]; }\n    src[o]=0;\n    n++;\n    int errored = 0;\n    for (int strict=0; strict<2; strict++) {\n      js_State *J = js_newstate(NULL, NULL, strict);\n      js_setreport(J, NULL);\n      if (js_ploadstring(J, \"[string]\", src)) { errored=1; js_pop(J,1); }\n      else { js_pushundefined(J); if (js_pcall(J,0)) errored=1; js_pop(J,1); }\n      js_freestate(J);\n    }\n    if (argc>2 && !errored) { printf(\"NOT-ERRORING: %s\\n\", line); bad++; }\n    if (argc<=2 && errored) { printf(\"ERRORS(unexpected for valid corpus): %s\\n\", line); bad++; }\n  }\n  printf(\"checked %d snippets, %d flagged\\n\", n, bad);\n  return 0;\n}\nEOF\ngcc -I c_src/include -o /tmp/chk /tmp/chk.c c_src/build/libmujs.so -lm -Wl,-rpath,$PWD/c_src/build\n# error corpora: pass a 2nd arg -> flags snippets that DO NOT error\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/errors_lexer.txt x\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/errors_parser_compiler.txt x\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/errors_runtime.txt x\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/errors_builtins.txt x\n# valid corpora: no 2nd arg -> flags snippets that DO error\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/builtins_regexp.txt\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/builtins_json.txt\n/tmp/chk translation/tests/corpus/builtins_date.txt\nEOF\n```\nIterate until the four `errors_*` files report `0 flagged`. For the three valid\ncorpora, a 