{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LuWQZR6PHo8BdBEomNSv6E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MuJS Error-Surface Table\n2\t\n3\tMechanically derived from `c_src/src/*.c`, `c_src/src/*.h`, `c_src/include/mujs.h`.\n4\tEvery row is one distinct rejection/error branch that the C source actually checks.\n5\t\n6\t## Legend\n7\t\n8\t**Error/sentinel conventions verified in the source:**\n9\t\n10\t* **regexp compile** — `js_regcompx()` / `js_regcomp()` install a `setjmp` landing pad\n11\t  (`regexp.c:903`). All compile-time rejections go through\n12\t  `static void die(struct cstate *g, const char *message)` which stores the static message\n13\t  string in `g->error` and `longjmp(g->kaboom, 1)` (`regexp.c:67-71`). The landing pad then\n14\t  does `if (errorp) *errorp = g.error;`, frees partial allocations, and **returns `NULL`**\n15\t  (`regexp.c:903-912`). On success `*errorp = NULL` and the `Reprog*` is returned\n16\t  (`regexp.c:984-985`). If `errorp == NULL` the message is discarded but `NULL` is still\n17\t  returned. `js_regcomp()` is just `regcompx(default_alloc, NULL, ...)` (`regexp.c:1007-1010`).\n18\t* **regexp match** — `js_regexec()` returns **`0` = match**, **`1` = no match**,\n19\t  **`-1` = recursion limit exceeded** (`regexp.c:1075-1076`, `regexp.c:1239`; the `-1` is\n20\t  produced by `match()` when `depth > REG_MAXREC`). There is no `errorp`.\n21\t* **regexp free** — `js_regfree(NULL)` / `js_regfreex(alloc, ctx, NULL)` are silent no-ops\n22\t  (`regexp.c:990`).\n23\t* **JS-level throws** — the `js_error` family is generated by the `DERROR` macro\n24\t  (`jserror.c:84-99`): `vsnprintf` into a **256-byte** `buf`, build an Error object of the\n25\t  matching prototype, then `js_throw(J)`. `js_throw()` unwinds to the innermost\n26\t  `js_try`/`js_savetry` frame via `longjmp` (`jsrun.c:1465-1477`). **If `J->trytop == 0` it\n27\t  calls `J->panic(J)` and then `abort()`** (`jsrun.c:1479-1481`). All `js_*error` functions\n28\t  are declared `JS_NORETURN` (`mujs.h:115-122`).\n29\t* **Internal \"raw literal\" throws** — `js_stackoverflow`, `js_trystackoverflow`,\n30\t  `js_outofmemory`, `js_runlimit` (`jsrun.c:14-42`) push a bare `JS_TLITSTR` string (not an\n31\t  Error object) and `js_throw`. Strings: `\"stack overflow\"`, `\"exception stack overflow\"`,\n32\t  `\"out of memory\"`, `\"script ran too long\"`.\n33\t* **Lexer / parser / compiler** — `jsY_error` (`jslex.c:6-21`), `jsP_error`\n34\t  (`jsparse.c:29-44`) and `jsC_error` (`jscompile.c:14-28`) all format\n35\t  `\"<filename>:<line>: <message>\"` into a 512-byte buffer (message part capped at 256 bytes\n36\t  by `vsnprintf(msgbuf, 256, ...)`), then `js_newsyntaxerror()` + `js_throw()`. So all of\n37\t  these surface as **SyntaxError** with a `file:line: ` prefix.\n38\t* **`p`-prefixed API** — `js_pcall`, `js_pconstruct` (`jsrun.c:1400-1425`),\n39\t  `js_ploadstring`, `js_dostring` (`jsstate.c:36-45`, `139-157`) return **`0` on success,\n40\t  `1` on error** with the error value left as the single value on the stack frame.\n41\t  `js_ptry()` (`jsstate.c:5-13`) is the pre-check that avoids `js_try` when the try stack is\n42\t  already full; it pushes the literal `\"exception stack overflow\"` and returns 1.\n43\t* **`try`-prefixed converters** — `js_trystring`/`js_trynumber`/`js_tryinteger`/\n44\t  `js_tryboolean` (`jsstate.c:47-109`) and `js_tryrepr` (`jsrepr.c:275-283`) swallow the\n45\t  throw and return the caller-supplied `error` fallback value.\n46\t* **Invalid stack indices are NOT errors** — `stackidx()` (`jsrun.c:219-225`) resolves\n47\t  `idx < 0 ? TOP+idx : BOT+idx` and, if the result is `< 0` or `>= TOP`, returns a pointer to\n48\t  a `static js_Value undefined`. So `js_type(J, 9999)` yields `JS_ISUNDEFINED`,\n49\t  `js_typeof(J, 9999)` yields `\"undefined\"`, and `js_getproperty(J, 9999, \"x\")` raises\n50\t  `TypeError \"cannot convert undefined to object\"` (`jsvalue.c:401`) rather than a stack error.\n51\t* **UTF-8 decode** — `jsU_chartorune` never fails: on malformed input it sets\n52\t  `*rune = Runeerror (0xFFFD)` and **returns 1** (`utf.c:127-129`).\n53\t* **`js_newstate`** returns **`NULL`** on allocation failure or on a throw during\n54\t  `jsB_init` (`jsstate.c:199`, `:217`, `:226`).\n55\t* **`assert()`** — 9 total in the library (see rows below); `NDEBUG` builds elide them.\n56\t\n57\t**Real limit constants (grepped, not guessed):**\n58\t\n59\t| constant | value | file:line |\n60\t|---|---|---|\n61\t| `JS_STACKSIZE` | 4096 | jsi.h:81 |\n62\t| `JS_ENVLIMIT` | 1024 | jsi.h:84 |\n63\t| `JS_TRYLIMIT` | 64 | jsi.h:87 |\n64\t| `JS_ARRAYLIMIT` | `1<<26` (67108864) | jsi.h:91 |\n65\t| `JS_GCFACTOR` | 5.0 | jsi.h:103 |\n66\t| `JS_ASTLIMIT` | 400 | jsi.h:107 |\n67\t| `JS_STRLIMIT` | `1<<28` (268435456) | jsi.h:111 |\n68\t| `js_Instruction` | `unsigned short` | jsi.h:119 |\n69\t| `REG_MAXSUB` | 16 | regexp.h:35 |\n70\t| `REPINF` | 255 | regexp.c:16 |\n71\t| `REG_MAXPROG` | `32<<10` (32768) | regexp.c:18 |\n72\t| `REG_MAXREC` | 4096 | regexp.c:21 |\n73\t| `REG_MAXSPAN` | 64 (→ 32 ranges/class) | regexp.c:24 |\n74\t| `REG_MAXCLASS` | 128 | regexp.c:27 |\n75\t| `UTFmax` / `Runeerror` / `Runemax` | 4 / 0xFFFD / 0x10FFFF | utf.h:79-83 |\n76\t| `maxExponent` (js_strtod) | 511 | jsdtoa.c:558 |\n77\t| `JS_REGEXP_G/I/M` | 1/2/4 | mujs.h:82-84 |\n78\t| `REG_ICASE/REG_NEWLINE/REG_NOTBOL` | 1/2/4 | regexp.h:23-28 |\n79\t| `JS_READONLY/DONTENUM/DONTCONF` | 1/2/4 | mujs.h:89-91 |\n80\t| `JS_STRICT` | 1 | mujs.h:77 |\n81\t\n82\t---\n83\t\n84\t## 1. `js_regcomp` / `js_regcompx` — compile rejections (all return `NULL`, set `*errorp`)\n85\t\n86\t| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n87\t|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n88\t| 1 | `js_regcomp` / `hex()` | `\\xZZ` or `\\uZZZZ` — escape digit not in `[0-9a-fA-F]` (regexp.c:101) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid escape sequence\"` |\n89\t| 2 | `js_regcomp` / `dec()` | `a{x}` — non-digit inside `{...}` quantifier (regexp.c:108) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid quantifier\"` |\n90\t| 3 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | pattern ends with a bare `\\` (regexp.c:127-128) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n91\t| 4 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | pattern ends with `\\c` (no control letter) (regexp.c:137-138) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n92\t| 5 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | `\\x` with fewer than 2 bytes remaining (regexp.c:142-143) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n93\t| 6 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | `\\u` with fewer than 4 bytes remaining (regexp.c:152-153) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated escape sequence\"` |\n94\t| 7 | `js_regcomp` / `nextrune()` | identity escape of a unicode letter or `_`, e.g. `\\q`, `\\_`, `\\é` — not in `ESCAPES \"BbDdSsWw^$\\\\.*+?()[]{}|-0123456789\"` (regexp.c:167-170) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid escape character\"` |\n95\t| 8 | `js_regcomp` / `lexcount()` | `{`-quantifier min reaches `REPINF` (255), e.g. `a{255}` (regexp.c:185-186) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"numeric overflow\"` |\n96\t| 9 | `js_regcomp` / `lexcount()` | `{`-quantifier max reaches `REPINF` (255), e.g. `a{1,255}` (regexp.c:199-200) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"numeric overflow\"` |\n97\t| 10 | `js_regcomp` / `newcclass()` | more than `REG_MAXCLASS` (128) character classes in one pattern (regexp.c:212-213) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"too many character classes\"` |\n98\t| 11 | `js_regcomp` / `addrange()` | range with `a > b`, e.g. `[z-a]` (regexp.c:223-224) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"invalid character class range\"` |\n99\t| 12 | `js_regcomp` / `addrange()` | more than `REG_MAXSPAN/2` = 32 disjoint spans in one class (`cc->end + 2 >= cc->spans + 64`) (regexp.c:252-253) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"too many character class ranges\"` |\n100\t| 13 | `js_regcomp` / `lexclass()` | EOF before closing `]`, e.g. `[abc` (regexp.c:321-322) | `NULL`, `*errorp = \"unterminated chara