(regexp.c:1075-1076) | returns **`-1`** (propagated up through I_SPLIT/I_PLA/I_NLA at regexp.c:1088, 1099, 1108) |\n129\t| 37 | `js_regexec` | pattern does not match `sp` | returns **`1`** (all \"no match\" branches in `match()`) |\n130\t| 38 | `js_regexec` | pattern matches | returns **`0`** (`case I_END: return 0;` regexp.c:1080-1081) |\n131\t| 39 | `js_regexec` | `sub == NULL` (regexp.c:1232-1233) | uses a stack-local `Resub scratch`; no crash, no error |\n132\t| 40 | `js_regexec` | always clears exactly `REG_MAXSUB` (16) slots and sets `sub->nsub = prog->nsub` (regexp.c:1235-1237) | callers must supply a `Resub` with 16 slots or memory is corrupted |\n133\t| 41 | `js_regexec` / `match()` | corrupt/unknown `pc->opcode` (`default:` arm) (regexp.c:1221-1222) | returns **`1`** (treated as no-match) |\n134\t| 42 | `js_regexec` / `I_REF` | back-reference whose group never matched → `out->sub[n].sp == NULL`, passed to `strncmp`/`strncmpcanon` with `i = 0` (regexp.c:1161-1167) | `i == 0` so `strncmp(sp, NULL, 0)` — length 0, no deref; falls through |\n135\t| 43 | `js_regfreex` | `prog == NULL` (regexp.c:990) | no-op, no crash |\n136\t| 44 | `js_regfree` | `prog == NULL` (regexp.c:1012-1015 → regexp.c:990) | no-op, no crash |\n137\t| 45 | `js_regfreex` | `prog->cclass == NULL` (no classes compiled) (regexp.c:991-992) | skips the cclass free; frees `start` and `prog` |\n138\t\n139\t## 3. `jsU_*` UTF-8 / Unicode (`utf.c`) — never throws, uses substitution/NULL sentinels\n140\t\n141\t| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n142\t|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n143\t| 46 | `jsU_chartorune` | input starts with the overlong NUL sequence `0xC0 0x80` (utf.c:58-61) | `*rune = 0`, returns **2** (deliberate CESU-style NUL) |\n144\t| 47 | `jsU_chartorune` | lead byte in `0x80..0xBF` (a bare continuation byte, `c < T2`) (utf.c:80-82) | `*rune = 0xFFFD`, returns **1** |\n145\t| 48 | `jsU_ch