{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bwakw47s5j2s7nupoccfflkcqxouajqpvk6j66cinbf4cf3i4nuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HV5L3618w6gEKWBFZ8qb4Z","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-jqRrno/translation/tests/corpus/builtins_regexp.txt","content":"# Phase B valid-path corpus -- RegExp construction, properties, exec/test and the\n# String.prototype methods that take a regexp, plus one snippet per pattern\n# construct that c_src/src/regexp.c actually implements.\n#\n# NOTHING HERE MAY THROW. The harness compares the stringified RESULT, so each\n# line ends in an expression whose value is informative (JSON.stringify or an\n# explicit String()/typeof where an array would flatten `undefined` to \"\").\n#\n# NOTE: the harness rewrites backslash+n -> newline, so a pattern that needs a\n# literal backslash-n is built with String.fromCharCode(10) / new RegExp(...).\n\n# --- construction: literal, one-arg, two-arg, from another RegExp ---\n/abc/.source\nnew RegExp('abc').source\nnew RegExp('abc', 'g').source\nRegExp('abc').source\nRegExp('abc', 'i').source\nnew RegExp(/abc/).source\nnew RegExp(/abc/gim).source\nString(new RegExp(/abc/gim))\nnew RegExp('').source\nnew RegExp().source\nString(new RegExp(''))\nnew RegExp('(?:)').source\n/(?:)/.source\nnew RegExp('a').constructor === RegExp\ntypeof /a/\nObject.prototype.toString.call(/a/)\n/a/ instanceof RegExp\n\n# --- all 8 combinations of g/i/m, via the literal form ---\n[/a/.global, /a/.ignoreCase, /a/.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/g.global, /a/g.ignoreCase, /a/g.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/i.global, /a/i.ignoreCase, /a/i.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/m.global, /a/m.ignoreCase, /a/m.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/gi.global, /a/gi.ignoreCase, /a/gi.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/gm.global, /a/gm.ignoreCase, /a/gm.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/im.global, /a/im.ignoreCase, /a/im.multiline].join(',')\n[/a/gim.global, /a/g