s/b08_numeric_torture.rs` | `js_itoa` over 60 000 ints incl. `INT_MIN`; `js_strtol` over every well-defined base 2..80; all five `jsV_numberto*` over ~67 000 doubles; `Number.prototype` formatting swept over ~120 extreme literals x every radix/precision |\n| P1 lexer helpers | 85-103 | `tests/b04_lexer_strhelpers.rs`, `tests/c12_internals.rs` | predicates exhaustive over `-300..0x110100` plus `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` and 30 000 random ints; `jsY_initlex`+`jsY_lex` token streams over 20 212 sources and `jsY_lexjson` over 10 112 |\n| P1 string helpers | 104-111 | `tests/b04_lexer_strhelpers.rs`, `tests/b08_numeric_torture.rs` | `js_isarrayindex` over 40 000 strings; `js_utflen`/`js_utfptrtoidx`/`js_runeat` over malformed and well-formed UTF-8 at every byte offset and index |\n| P2 regexp | 112-248 | `tests/b03_regexp.rs`, `tests/b07_random.rs` | every construct x all 4 `cflags` x all 2 `eflags` x 45 subjects (61 232 cases); all 1-byte and a large 2-byte/3-byte pattern space (34 134); 78 084 random patterns; 156 056 random subjects; 21 280 cases through the JS `RegExp` API incl. all 8 flag combos and `lastIndex` bookkeeping; custom-allocator entry points compared down to allocation call counts |\n| P3 state / allocator / limits | 249-281 | `tests/b05_stackapi.rs` | custom `js_Alloc` with a non-NULL `actx` compared by exact allocation counts and byte totals, plus an allocation-failure sweep; `js_setlimit` run/mem matrix; `js_gc` with every `report` value; abort paths compared across processes |\n| P3 strict mode | 282-309 | `tests/corpus/strict_mode.txt`, `tests/b06_scripts.rs`, `tests/c11_corpus_all.rs` | 106 snippets, each run in BOTH modes so the mode-dependent difference itself is compared |\n| P3 property attributes | 310-323 | `tests/b05_stackapi.rs`, `tests/c09_api_errors.rs` | all 8 `atts` combinations plus out-of-range bits (8, -1, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`), each followed by overwrite / redefine / enumerate / delete |\n| P3 value & data shapes | 324-356 | `tests/b05_sta