FIGS.md`** — 424 contiguous rows, all `[x]`, each with a coverage entry naming its test. Coverage is exhaustive where feasible (all 65 536 two-byte UTF-8 sequences; every Unicode code point through every UCD table; all 4 × 2 regexp flag combinations × every construct) and property-style with fixed seeds elsewhere.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 445 contiguous rows with a per-section coverage map. Error *messages* are compared, not just failure. 13 rows are C-side UB with no comparable result — listed in `UNCHECKED_UB_ROWS` and asserted present, not silently skipped; 4 rows end in `abort()` in both builds and are compared **across processes** (exit status, signal, stderr).\n- **Feature combinations** — the crate declares no `[features]` and contains no `#[cfg]`, so `check_feature_combos.sh` proves that from `Cargo.toml`/`src/` and still runs default, `--no-default-features` and `--all-features`: **ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASS**.\n\n**195 tests / 15 targets / 0 failures / 0 warnings, ≈14.65 million compared cases.**\n\nTwo notes on the setup: the C `.so` is linked without `-lm`, so the harness publishes libm into the global symbol namespace at load time rather than touching `c_src/`; and `.cargo/config.toml` sets `offline = true` because the sandbox blocks crates.io (`libloading` 0.8.9 was already cached). Nothing under `c_src/` was modified.\n\nThree C-side UB findings surfaced along the way and are documented in `ERRORS.md` — most notably `js_strtol` with `base > 80`, where the digit table's sentinel `80` also covers the NUL terminator, so the scan runs off the end of the string."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1286,"cache_read_input_tokens":551555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1286,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"365846c7-7961-47ff-8218-f2422469d650","uuid":"09509d3c-12